    "https://myapps.northcarolina.edu/hr/careers/": {
      "title": "Individually Remarkable & Collectively Extraordinary",
      "description": "Careers | Human Resources Careers Policies and Forms SHRA Policies EHRA Policies UNC Policy Manual UNC System Office Policies, Procedures and Forms About HR Staff Directory Organization Chart Reporting Concerns and Complaints Institution HR Contacts News and Announcements Contact HR Sign In Select Page Individually Remarkable & Collectively Extraordinary That’s how we describe our UNC System institutions and affiliates across North Carolina, including the great team we have at the UNC System Office. Come join us! External candidates: Search open positions Current System Office / PBS NC / NCSEAA / Arboretum employees: Search open positions Your Career & Our Collective Mission In North Carolina, all the public educational institutions granting four-year degrees are part of the University of North Carolina System . Our multi-campus system encompasses 16 universities; the NC School of Science and Mathematics, the nation’s first public residential high school for gifted students; and a number of affiliated institutions, including PBS North Carolina, the North Carolina State Education Authority, and UNC Health. The UNC System Office, located in Raleigh, houses the offices of the System’s president and senior administrative staff . These core administrative divisions provide a comprehensive array of operational services and System-wide guidance in academic affairs, business and financial management, long-range planning, human resources, information technology, legal affairs, and external relations. Fulfilling the role of the UNC System Office requires a variety of skills. Our openings range from accounting to instruction, program management, IT support, and many more. No matter their positions, though, our staff are united in working toward a single purpose: serving North Carolina and its citizens by supporting the teaching, research, and public service work at our institutions, which in turn helps ensure that our students receive an excellent and affordable education. Find out more about us About UNC System Office Benefits & Well-being About the Area Apply Now! External candidates: Search open positions Institution and affiliate open positions Follow UNC System Office on social media to learn more about our institutions and our mission! Follow Follow Follow Follow Follow About UNC System Human Resources The UNC System Office of Human Resources provides centralized leadership and support to the human resources offices of the 17 constituent institutions of the University of North Carolina System and provides human resource services to UNC System Office staff. Contact Us UNC System Human Resources UNC System Office 223 South West Street, Suite 1700 Raleigh, NC 27603 SystemHR@northcarolina.edu T: (919) 843-5293 F: (984) 777-9055 Quicklinks UNC System Office website UNC System Directory Job Postings (UNC System Office) Job Postings (UNC Institutions) Website Access Requests Reporting Concerns and Complaints The university is committed to providing services that are accessible to everyone. We continually update our website and review it with the aim of meeting users’ accessibility needs. If you or someone you know encounters a barrier to the information you need, please report accessibility barrier using this form."
    },
    "https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/all_jobs.atom": {
      "title": "University of North Carolina",
      "description": "tag:spartantalent.uncg.edu,2005:/postings/all_jobs University of North Carolina at Greensboro: All Jobs 2026-09-04T15:10:50-04:00 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35903 2026-09-04T15:10:49-04:00 2026-09-04T15:10:50-04:00 Assistant Director - Regional Recruiter (Raleigh/Wake County) <div><strong>Re-Post, Previous Applicants Need Not Re-Apply, Still Under Consideration<br></strong><br>The Assistant Director will focus on both high school student recruitment as well as community college transfer recruitment. This position will recruit and cultivate prospects, applicants, and admitted students through direct participation in a variety of activities designed to educate and inspire prospective students, parents, and counselors. The position will also evaluate credentials and make independent decisions regarding admission to UNCG. The position will build relationships in high school and community college spaces designed to enhance UNCG’s brand awareness and reputation. Finally, the position will positively affect admitted students’ decisions to matriculate to UNCG.</div> Undergraduate Admissions - 10202 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35790 2026-08-21T09:02:05-04:00 2026-08-21T09:02:05-04:00 Director, Marketing Strategy <div>The Director of Marketing Strategy is a senior strategic leader and subject matter expert within the University Communications’ Brand Marketing team, overseeing an integrated marketing strategy vertical that supports the goals of institutional brand awareness and enrollment priorities. Reporting to the Executive Director of Brand Marketing, this position leads the development, coordination, and evaluation of marketing strategies across paid and owned channels, ensuring that the university's marketing investments are data-informed, audience-centered, brand-consistent, and aligned with institutional goals.</div><div><br>The Director provides strategic oversight for integrated marketing planning and execution across paid advertising, web content management, SEO and GEO, and organic and paid social media. This position guides campaign strategy, ad planning and execution, audience segmentation, channel coordination, performance measurement, and ongoing optimization. The Director leads a team of marketing professionals, establishing clear priorities, shared standards, and integrated workflows that support effective execution across the full marketing enterprise.<br><br></div><div><strong><br></strong><br></div> University Communications - 33901 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35312 2026-07-01T00:01:12-04:00 2026-07-01T00:01:16-04:00 Shuttle Bus Driver <div>Parking Operations and Campus Access Management are seeking qualified applicants on a <strong>temporary basis for entry-level</strong> <strong>Vehicle/Equipment Operator positions</strong> that may come available. Duties include:</div><ul><li>Responsibility for operating a bus on assigned route and schedule</li><li>to provide safe and efficient transportation of students, faculty, and staff.</li><li>Work involves: Performing pre-and post-trip inspections of the bus and reporting mechanical defects or failures to the Transportation Manager.</li><li>Obeying all traffic laws and University regulations while operating the bus Creating a customer service-oriented environment for users.</li><li>Employee will be responsible for completing all required reports and securing the vehicle before leaving.</li></ul><div><strong>When the Department temporarily needs a Vehicle/Equipment Operator, they will consider applicants that have applied to this temp pool.</strong></div> Human Resources - 58401 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/34428 2026-03-17T09:53:38-04:00 2026-03-17T09:53:39-04:00 Academic Professional - Three College Observatory <div>The College of Arts &amp; Sciences at the University of North Carolina at Greensboro invites applications for a 12-month professional track faculty position of Academic Professional Assistant Professor (AP) to begin on August 1, 2026. The position will have an initial one-year appointment with the possibility of renewal. The AP will be responsible for oversight and maintenance of equipment at the university’s Three College Observatory (including a 0.8 meter optical telescope, CCD camera, and echelle spectrograph) as well as a small analog Spitz planetarium on the UNCG campus. The position is expected to teach seven introductory courses during the year (spread out over fall, spring, and two summer sessions).<br><br></div> Physics and Astronomy - 12213 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35854 2026-08-31T14:48:50-04:00 2026-08-31T14:48:51-04:00 SBTDC Business Counselor <div>The University of North Carolina at Greensboro (UNCG) invites applications for a Small Business and Technology Development Center (SBTDC) Business Counselor. This position is funded through the North Carolina Small Business and Technology Development Center and is housed within Innovate UNCG, the university's hub for innovation, entrepreneurship, commercialization, and economic development.<br><br></div><div>The SBTDC Business Counselor serves as a strategic resource for faculty innovators, research scholars, student entrepreneurs, university-affiliated startups, and small business clients seeking to launch, grow, or commercialize new ventures. The position provides business counseling, technical assistance, market research support, and entrepreneurial education to help clients advance innovative ideas, research-based technologies, and business opportunities.<br><br></div><div>Working closely with the Director of Innovate UNCG, university faculty, students, regional partners, and the statewide SBTDC network, the Business Counselor will strengthen UNCG's innovation ecosystem by supporting entrepreneurship, technology commercialization, startup development, and economic growth throughout the region. The position serves as an important bridge between the university's research enterprise, entrepreneurial community, and North Carolina's broader economic development ecosystem.</div> LaunchUNCG - 11506 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35594 2026-08-03T07:56:53-04:00 2026-08-03T07:56:54-04:00 Collaboration Coordinator - Special populations <div>The Collaboration Coordinator-Special Populations will foster collaboration and advocate for Family Voice &amp; Choice in partnership with other service delivery systems, State agencies, and other relevant stakeholders, including the Department of Public Instruction and SAMHSA-sponsored national agencies with a focus on historically underserved populations in NC.<br><br></div><div>The Collaboration Coordinator also will work to establish a formal network or directory of different family, youth, and/or young-adult led organizations or roles within organizations across the State. This network or directory will help to facilitate future additional collaboration and coordination of individuals working to elevate the voice and perspectives of families, youths, and young adults across the state and help to make it easier than it is currently to identify who is engaged in this work throughout North Carolina.<br><br></div><div>The dedicated Coordination and Collaboration role within the Family and Youth Support and Education Program will be critical to the program’s ability to support local and State Collaboratives, while also remaining true to the SOC Values and Principles.</div> Center-Youth-Families & Comm - 11504 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35334 2026-07-06T15:29:56-04:00 2026-07-06T15:29:57-04:00 Assistant Professor, Accounting <div>The Bryan School of Business and Economics at the University of North Carolina at Greensboro is seeking qualified applications for a tenure stream position at the rank of <strong>Assistant Professor </strong>(tenure-track) in the Department of Accounting and Finance beginning August 1, 2027.<br><br></div><div>The University emphasizes high quality in research and teaching, and teaching responsibilities will primarily be at the undergraduate level and will include both online and face-to-face instruction. Service to the University and to the academic and/or practicing professions is also expected.<br><br></div><div>Screening of applications shall begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.<br><br></div> Accounting and Finance - 11812 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35798 2026-08-21T10:16:01-04:00 2026-08-21T10:16:03-04:00 Sr. Systems Engineer <div>The Infrastructure Team Lead serves as the senior technical leader for the Enterprise Systems Infrastructure Engineering and Architecture team in the Information Technology Services department, providing strategic direction, technical expertise, and operational oversight for enterprise infrastructure platforms and services. This position leads and mentors technical staff, coordinates team priorities, and ensures the reliability, security, and continuous improvement of infrastructure systems that support the University's mission. The team is responsible for delivering modern systems and storage infrastructure facilitating further solution development. This position is responsible for architecting cloud infrastructure and managing cloud and storage assets. This position is expected to be an expert in cloud technologies, must be capable of working with the latest cloud technologies, and provides technical leadership through cloud architecture.<br><br>The Systems Engineering and Architecture team is part of the Enterprise Technology Infrastructure group that strives to connect, enable, and empower people through technology that transforms the University and the region. This position is eligible for full-time telework.</div> Info Technology Services - 23101 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/34571 2026-04-01T00:22:58-04:00 2026-04-01T00:23:01-04:00 Coordinator for Student Athletic Support Services <div>These services will include, but are not limited to: provide intense monitoring and academic support for student-athletes, assist with student-athlete specific course registration, assist in the academic coaching of student-athletes for designated assigned sport programs, develop and oversee programming/initiatives/events, participate in recruiting visits with prospective student-athletes, and other duties as assigned.<br><br></div><div>The Coordinator will interpret, analyze and monitor the academic progress of student-athletes; assess student-athlete overall academic performance and its impact on progress toward graduation and NCAA eligibility; maintain knowledge of all NCAA and University rules concerning academic standing and eligibility requirements.<br><br></div><div>In addition, the Coordinator will also be responsible for assisting the Assistant AD for Student-Athlete Support Services (SASS) with the coordination of Student Development and implementation of the Spartan Shield Program. The coordinator will serve as the Student-Athlete Advisory Committee (SAAC) Advisor.</div> Intercollegiate Athletics - 85001 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35856 2026-09-01T07:42:24-04:00 2026-09-01T07:42:25-04:00 Early Childhood Teacher Assistant <div>Early Childhood Education Teachers Assistants in the Child Care Education Program will work in a classroom as part of the consistent teaching team. They are responsible for assisting the Lead Teacher with curriculum planning in classrooms for young children, maintaining licensing and accreditation standards, creating a respectful high-quality classroom environment, caregiving routines, classroom activities, supervising groups of children indoors and outdoors, and light housekeeping duties such as serving or cleaning after meals.</div> Human Devlp and Family Studies - 12403 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35639 2026-08-10T07:23:28-04:00 2026-08-10T07:23:29-04:00 Assistant Professor of Media Production <div>The Department of Media Studies at UNC Greensboro invites applications for a Tenure-Track<strong> </strong>Assistant Professor of Media Production with an emphasis on Virtual Production and Emerging Media to begin August 1, 2027. This position focuses on Media Production with a specific emphasis on Emerging Media technologies. In addition to filmmaking, this position includes other media production with emerging media technologies. The successful candidate will have an established record in creative work and/or scholarship and have experience in Virtual Production and/or the integration of Cinematic AI applications within the curriculum. The successful candidate should be able to teach undergraduate courses related to media production. Courses will include Introduction to Media Production and screenwriting at the fundamental level, as well as upper-level courses (e.g., cinematography, directing, editing, lighting, sound, producing). The successful candidate will be expected to engage in teaching, professional growth and development activity (e.g., research/scholarship, creative activity, and/or professional practice), and service at the Department, College, and/or University levels.</div> Media Studies - 12226 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35405 2026-07-13T14:36:05-04:00 2026-07-13T14:36:06-04:00 Senior Financial Aid Counselor <div>The Senior Financial Aid Counselor serves as a resource for resolving complex financial aid issues and provides advanced support to students, families, and frontline staff. This position works closely with leadership to research challenging cases, interpret regulations, and determine appropriate resolutions. The Senior Counselor administers the Emergency Loan Program, assists with Return to Title IV (R2T4) reviews, and helps ensure compliance with all applicable federal, state, and institutional regulations. The position works closely with the Senior Assistant Director for Counseling Services to support the onboarding, training, and mentorship of new and current front-line counselors. This is a student-facing role that requires strong communication, critical thinking, problem-solving, and customer service skills.</div> Financial Aid - 10208 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/23172 2022-06-03T15:02:52-04:00 2022-06-03T15:02:53-04:00 Elder Law Adjunct Instructor (Temporary) <div>The Gerontology Program in the Department of Social Work invites applications for an adjunct instructor in the graduate Gerontology program. We are seeking a dynamic and experienced professional with expertise in elder law to teach our <em>Elder Law for Gerontological Professionals</em> course. The online course is taught over a 7.5-week period from August through October.</div><div><br>Duties and responsibilities of the position include:</div><ul><li>Instruct and guide the class in an efficient and effective manner</li><li>Use course materials in Canvas effectively</li><li>Maintain accurate records of student work and attendance</li><li>Maintain a safe and orderly learning environment</li><li>Grade and return student work in a timely manner</li><li>Counsel students regarding their grades and progress in the course</li><li>Comply with the university’s professional development procedures for online instructors</li></ul> Social Work - 12401 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35807 2026-08-24T14:34:04-04:00 2026-08-24T14:34:04-04:00 Administrative Support Specialist <div>This position, housed in the Dean’s Office, will provide support to several areas within the School of Education without administrative support. This position will offer support to School of Education's Dean's Office, Business Office, Office of Student Success, and Spartan Education Scholars Program. Other duties include initiating personnel actions, budgeting (including processing all payments and travel reimbursements), event planning, customer service, and other office activities.</div> Dean's Office - ED - 12001 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35650 2026-08-11T08:17:55-04:00 2026-08-11T08:17:56-04:00 Project Manager (Journey) <div>This position is responsible for comprehensive and simultaneous Project Management of multiple UNCG projects of various sizes. Projects will range in value from less than $30K up to and potentially exceeding the $4M threshold for full NC State Construction Office oversight. The purpose and intent of this position is to execute the following duties for assigned projects: (a) act as agent for the department maintaining responsibility for customer relations and customer satisfaction; (b) perform pre-design, advance planning, or programming services as demanded by the project requirements; and © provide management and oversight of contracted design and construction services. Duties shall be as necessitated by project requirements and may include, but are not limited to: writing and creating project related technical scoping documents for customers and consultants; development and management of project schedules and budgets; technical review of construction documents; oversight and management of construction activities in the field. Implicitly within these duties are administrative tasks associated with the formation of contracts, processing of payments, and maintenance of project records in digital and hard copy formats.</div> Facilities D&C-Departmental - 56411 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/34777 2026-04-27T17:06:40-04:00 2026-04-27T17:06:41-04:00 Lecturer in Information Systems <div>The <strong>Department of Information Systems and Supply Chain Management</strong> (ISSCM) in the Bryan School of Business at the University of North Carolina Greensboro (UNCG) invites applications, expressions of interest, and nominations for a non-tenure track position in Information System/Information Technology/Business Analytics/Cybersecurity/Artificial Intelligence. The position will commence on August 1, 2026, at the rank of <strong>Lecturer</strong> (non-tenure track).<br><br></div><div>The full- time position is responsible for instruction and must be prepared to teach face-to-face and online courses, as needed by the Department. Teaching online courses is required, and service to the university and to the academic and/or practicing professions is also expected. This position does not carry any research expectations.<br><br></div><div>The successful candidate will serve as a bridge between the Bryan School and the business community. We expect this person to be instrumental in securing internships and job placements for our students by collaborating with businesses. Prior experience working with the business community to create career opportunities for students is a major asset for this position.<br><br></div> Info Sys and Supply Chn Mngmt - 11806 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35870 2026-09-02T00:00:44-04:00 2026-09-02T00:00:47-04:00 Assistant Professor of Psychology <div>The Department of Psychology at UNC Greensboro invites applications for a tenure-track position in Social Psychology (Assistant Professor) to begin August 1, 2027.</div><div>We seek someone to join an active and collaborative department. The Department of Psychology consists of 28 full-time faculty and offers a BA and BS in psychology, including Disciplinary Honors, an MA in experimental psychology, and a PhD in clinical, cognitive, developmental, and social psychology (see <a href=\"https://psy.uncg.edu/\"><strong>https://psy.uncg.edu/</strong></a> for more information).</div><div>The doctoral program in Social Psychology consists of four faculty who provide individualized training in research and statistical methods. We have ongoing expertise on topics such as close relationships, social cognition, social perception, motivation, self and identity, and aesthetics/creativity.</div><div>We welcome applications from any area of social/personality psychology. We are especially interested in candidates with expertise in both of the following topics: health/well-being and social cognition. More specifically, we seek scholars who study how people think, reason, and make health-related decisions as well as decisions that may more broadly affect their environments and social worlds. The successful candidate will also be expected to contribute coursework and research experiences to an interdisciplinary BA in Health, Medicine, and Society (HMS).</div><div>All applicants should show evidence of a strong independent research program, potential for external funding, a commitment to working with students from diverse backgrounds, and potential for excellence in graduate and undergraduate teaching. Candidates must hold or anticipate a PhD in psychology or a related field by August 1, 2027.</div> Psychology - 12215 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35423 2026-07-15T00:01:11-04:00 2026-07-15T00:01:13-04:00 Technical Coordinator <div>The UNCG School of Dance seeks a Dance Technical Coordinator for a full-time (100%) 9 month- appointment to oversee all production aspects for the school. The successful candidate will demonstrate a thorough understanding of the technical and artistic aspects of lighting and production for dance and possess strong artistic collaboration skills. Primary duties will include designing lights for faculty and student choreographic works, instructing undergraduate and graduate Dance Production courses, and managing undergraduate student stage crew practicums.</div><div>Within the context of UNCG’s comprehensive liberal arts curriculum, the UNCG School of Dance offers bachelor’s and master’s degrees that provide specialized skills for a variety of careers in the developing field of dance. Within the UNC System, the UNCG School of Dance is positioned as the training ground for the thinking dancer, who values the rigors of both praxis and scholarship and celebrates a variety of approaches to dancing, dance making, and dance as a way of knowing.</div> School of Dance - 13004 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/27073 2023-08-17T17:13:04-04:00 2023-08-17T17:13:05-04:00 Student Support Facilitator <div>This position will be 1:1 (peer to peer) student support for 15 hours per week with 5 hours per week of administrative support and/or planning/scheduling. This position works directly with students (with intellectual disabilities) enrolled in the Integrative Community Studies (ICS)/Beyond Academics Certificate program. Examples of support provided may include (but are not limited to) academic support, social skills support, and/or living skills support.</div> Comp Trans and Post-Sec Edu - 11514 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35828 2026-08-27T09:44:37-04:00 2026-08-27T09:44:38-04:00 Program Assistant - Scheduling Coordinator <div>This position is pivotal in fostering a culture of excellence, demonstrating strong leadership, and significantly impacting the organization’s overall efficiency and effectiveness by supporting NCRLAP staff. The key responsibilities include additional leadership assignments (55%), schedule assessments (25%), budget and financial management (15%), and other duties (5%).</div> Human Devlp and Family Studies - 12403 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35681 2026-08-12T12:59:10-04:00 2026-08-12T12:59:11-04:00 Systems and Infrastructure Generalist <div>Reporting to the Assistant Registrar for Systems and Infrastructure, the Systems and Infrastructure Generalist is a member of the Registrar’s Systems and Reporting team and serves within the University Registrar’s Office (URO) as the webmaster, report support, data specialist, and systems technician. This position actively participates in implementing and testing new tools, workflow processes, and strategic initiatives designed to increase departmental effectiveness. The Systems Infrastructure Generalist is primarily responsible for technological, systems, and reporting-running functions within the URO, including their interdependence with university-wide systems, and provides functional support for the Systems and Reporting Team.<br><br></div><div>In addition to these responsibilities, the Systems and Infrastructure Generalist will be trained in the scribing and maintenance of DegreeWorks, the University’s degree clearance and auditing system. Scribing is an essential skill set within the URO and requires a higher level of technical skill, understanding, and ability. The position requires a solid understanding of how to leverage reporting to support student needs and the institution’s strategic goals. The Systems and Infrastructure Generalist will also assist in troubleshooting system issues, maintaining system documentation, and supporting the integration of new technologies and processes across the office.</div> University Registrar's Office - 10204 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35017 2026-06-01T16:14:02-04:00 2026-06-01T16:14:03-04:00 Associate Vice Chancellor of Enrollment Management <div>Associate Vice Chancellor of Enrollment, reporting directly to the Vice Chancellor of Enrollment plays a critical leadership role within the division by serving as second in command for the division and serving as the primary leader in the absence of the Vice Chancellor. In partnership with the VCEM, the AVC will lead the development, execution, and assessment of enrollment and financial aid strategies for all new undergraduates and will work directly with the Deans on enrollment planning at the College/Unit/School level. The AVC will be responsible for guiding a state-of-the art new student recruitment approach that includes selecting and implementing enrollment technologies that advance the ability to make data-informed decisions and measurable resource planning. This includes yield optimization modeling, financial aid leveraging optimization, CPOS implementation, and strategic communication across audience types. The AVC will lead metrics-driven key decisions related to the development and execution of enrollment plans and programs.</div> Enrollment Management - 10207 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35872 2026-09-02T08:11:19-04:00 2026-09-02T08:11:20-04:00 Organic Chemistry - Tenure Track, Assistant Professor <div>The Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry at the University of North Carolina at Greensboro is seeking to fill a tenure-track faculty position in the area of Organic Chemistry at the rank of Assistant Professor with an anticipated start date of August 2027. Research interests involving synthesis that tie directly into UNCG’s priorities of health/medicine or energy/sustainable chemistry are preferred. A PhD in Chemistry, Organic Chemistry, or Medicinal Chemistry is a requirement for the position. Applicants should demonstrate a solid record of accomplishment in publications and should show promise for establishing an independent and externally funded research program. Applicants will be expected to mentor master’s and doctoral research students, and to contribute to the department’s long-standing strength in undergraduate research. Additionally, the successful hire will demonstrate teaching excellence at both the graduate and undergraduate levels. A competitive start up package will be provided.<br><br></div><div>Applications must be submitted through Spartan Talent. To apply, visit <a href=\"https://jobsearch.uncg.edu\"><strong>https://jobsearch.uncg.edu</strong></a> and click on “Faculty/Tenure Stream and apply to position 1105. Applicants should upload a cover letter addressed to Dr. Nicholas Oberlies, Committee Chair, a curriculum vita (CV), a description of proposed research, a teaching statement and identify at least three (3) contacts who will send a letter of recommendation. Any technical questions concerning the application submission process can be addressed to Trina Porcher at <a href=\"mailto:t_porche@uncg.edu\"><strong>t_porche@uncg.edu</strong></a>. Review of application will begin 10/01/2026 and will continue until the position is filled.<br><br>UNCG is a Minority Serving Institution. UNCG and the Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry foster an environment of collaboration across departments and schools and support community-engaged research. UNCG is located in Greensboro, the largest city in North Carolina’s Piedmont Triad region and the third-most populous city in the state. Greensboro is a vibrant city with nearly 300,000 residents and more than 47,000 college students and is known for its expansive parks and greenway system, arts, music, and sports.&nbsp;</div> Chemistry & Biochemistry - 12205 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35432 2026-07-16T08:18:33-04:00 2026-07-16T08:18:34-04:00 Digital Media Commons and Makerspace Department Manager <div>The Digital Media Commons and Makerspace Department Manager provides strategic leadership for the vision, development, and operations of the department by guiding the growth of programs, services, facilities, technologies, and training in collaboration with DMC staff, library leadership, and campus partners. The Manager oversees all aspects of departmental operations; develops and implements departmental policies and procedures in collaboration with DMC staff and library leadership; and supervises full-time and temporary department personnel, ensuring the successful implementation of departmental policies and procedures and high-quality administration of programs and services. The hours for this position are Monday – Friday 8 am – 5 pm, with occasional night and weekend hours based on departmental need.</div> University Libraries - 11601 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/29503 2024-06-26T10:57:43-04:00 2024-06-26T10:57:44-04:00 Post Doctoral Fellow <div>This position is expected to perform research in the area of alcohol-related organ injury. The research projects aim at understanding the cellular and molecular mechanisms of alcohol-induced pathogenesis at the gut-liver axis and exploring preventive and/or therapeutic interventions. Data generated from the projects will be used to support external funding applications.</div> Ctr for Transl Biomed Research - 13403 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35833 2026-08-28T14:33:55-04:00 2026-08-28T14:33:56-04:00 Assistant Professor of Statistics <div>The Department of Mathematics and Statistics at the University of North Carolina at Greensboro (UNCG) invites applications for a tenure-track position in Statistics at the rank of Assistant Professor beginning August 1, 2027.<br><br>The department seeks candidates with strong potential for research and teaching in statistics. Applicants whose research interests include machine learning, artificial intelligence, data science or biostatistics are preferred, but strong applicants in all research areas will be considered.</div><div>The successful candidate will be expected to establish and maintain an active program of research and scholarship, pursue opportunities for external funding, teach undergraduate and graduate courses in statistics, advise and mentor students, and contribute appropriate service to the department, university, and profession. Opportunities exist for interdisciplinary research and collaboration across the university and with external partners. The successful candidate will also mentor students in UNCG's growing B.S. in Statistics and M.S. in Applied Statistics programs, including supervision of undergraduate research and M.S. Capstone projects.</div> Mathematics and Statistics - 12227 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35710 2026-08-17T15:03:16-04:00 2026-08-17T15:03:17-04:00 Assistant Director of Grounds <div>The primary purpose of this position is to provide overall management of all activities related to grounds maintenance. The primary duties are:<br><br></div><div>25% Oversight of Turf Maintenance including recreational and athletic fields<br>25% Oversight of Tree and Shrub Maintenance throughout campus including UNCG’s Peabody Park<br>20% Oversight of Irrigation Repair and Installation<br>10% Oversight of Preventive Maintenance and Repairs on Grounds Equipment<br>10% Oversight of Fertilizer and Pesticide Application throughout campus<br>5% Oversight of Safety Training for grounds staff<br>5% Oversight of General Overall Campus Grounds Upkeep, Cleanup and tidiness<br><br><strong>This position is a mandatory position as defined in the Adverse Weather and Emergency Event Policy.</strong></div> Facilities Operations - 56404 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35201 2026-06-19T00:01:01-04:00 2026-06-19T00:01:05-04:00 Post Doctoral Fellow <div>We are seeking applicants for a postdoctoral scholar position in the Denning-Jannace research group. The project will focus on synthesizing light activated ruthenium complexes for antifungal and antibiofilm activity with an emphasis on interruption of metal homeostatic pathways. Applicants with a strong background in bioinorganic chemistry, inorganic synthesis of light active complexes, or biology of human fungal pathogens are encouraged to apply. Most importantly we are looking for someone with enthusiasm for science and research, so applications from exceptional individuals who have a different scientific focus within fields related to different aspects of inorganic chemistry, biochemistry/chemical biology, or fungal biology are more than welcome. Candidates will have the opportunity to work in an interdisciplinary environment and have close interactions with other team members with diverse backgrounds in a variety of areas including bioinorganic chemistry, inorganic synthesis, bioanalytical chemistry, fungal biology, and chemical biology to broaden their skills.</div> Chemistry & Biochemistry - 12205 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35886 2026-09-03T08:18:27-04:00 2026-09-03T08:18:28-04:00 Administrative Assistant <div>**Re-Post, Previous Applicants Need Not Re-Apply, Still Under Consideration<br><br>The Advanced Administrative Assistant provides high-level administrative and operational support to the Office of University Communications and its senior leadership. This position requires substantial independent judgment, advanced organizational skills, and the ability to manage complex, often confidential tasks across a dynamic communications and marketing environment. The Advanced Administrative Assistant serves as a key resource for staff as well as for faculty, students, and external stakeholders, and is expected to exercise initiative, discretion, and professionalism at all times.</div> University Communications - 33901 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35838 2026-08-31T00:00:43-04:00 2026-08-31T00:00:44-04:00 Assistant Professor of Communication Sciences and Disorders <div>The faculty member will be an integral part of the undergraduate and master’s programs in the department. Preference will be given to applicants with teaching and research expertise in dysphagia and motor speech disorders. Interest and experience in TBI, dementia, and voice disorders will also be considered.</div> Comm Sciences and Disorders - 13001 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35461 2026-07-20T16:32:49-04:00 2026-07-20T16:32:50-04:00 Lead Accounts Payable Specialist <div>This position is critical to the University’s Accounts Payable operations and supports the timely, accurate, and compliant processing of vendor invoices, employee reimbursements, supplier onboarding activities, and other disbursement functions. The role serves as a key resource for ensuring compliance with University, UNC System, State, and Federal policies while supporting campus departments in navigating increasingly automated financial processes.<br><br></div><div>As Accounts Payable operations have evolved through the implementation of PaymentWorks, Chrome River, Jaggaer, electronic workflows, and supplier self-service tools, the responsibilities of this position have expanded beyond transactional processing to include policy interpretation, campus training, audit support, vendor management, issue resolution, and process improvement. The position plays an important role in maintaining internal controls, mitigating compliance risks, and supporting the University’s financial stewardship responsibilities.</div> Office of the Controller - 56202 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/31449 2025-03-07T15:44:19-05:00 2025-03-07T15:44:20-05:00 Certified Registered Nurse Anesthetist Faculty <div>The School of Nursing at the University of North Carolina at Greensboro is recruiting for a certified registered nurse anesthetist faculty member in the Doctor of Nursing Practice (DNP) program. We are seeking an innovative and talented individual who is actively engaged in evidence-based practice and education and who wants to advance the teaching, service, and scholarship/research mission of the UNCG School of Nursing.<br><br></div><div>Responsibilities of the position include teaching, active contribution to scholarship through evidence-based practice; student supervision and advising including participation in DNP capstone projects; and service to the school, university and community/profession.<br><br></div><div>The academic appointment is a 12-month clinical track position with full benefits with an August 1, 2025, start date. Review of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.<br><br>Part-time CRNA faculty positions are also available. For information about part-time positions, please reach out to Dr. Wanda Williams, Department Chair and Program Director for Advanced Nursing Education, at wmwilliams@uncg.edu.</div> Dean's Office - NU - 12801 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35721 2026-08-18T11:24:25-04:00 2026-08-18T11:24:26-04:00 Exhibition Designer/Preparator <div>This position supports the Weatherspoon Art Museum’s priorities through the timely and thorough completion of all aspects of collections care and exhibition installation. This includes handling, preparing, installing, storing, packing, and shipping artwork. In consultation with the museum curators, the exhibition designer/ preparator participates in exhibition design, scheduling, and layout. This individual executes safe handling and movement of artwork to support teaching with the collections. They lead the design and production of exhibition and print materials that support the museum’s programs, ensuring a consistent, sophisticated, and mission-aligned visual presence across all collections and exhibition touchpoints. They also contribute design support to exhibitions at the Jeanne Tannenbaum Center for Creative Practice. The position reports to the registrar and works in close collaboration with the museum preparator on most tasks. All Museums and Creative Practice staff support the associate vice chancellor in developing a vibrant and engaged community.</div> Weatherspoon Art Museum - 11001 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35234 2026-06-23T16:24:57-04:00 2026-06-23T16:24:58-04:00 Assistant Director <div>The Assistant Director for Loan Processing role requires the coordination and administration of the Federal Direct Loan Program, private education loan processing, award generation/revisions, verification of the appropriate disbursement of loan funds, and ensuring that loan eligibility is maintained throughout the financial aid process. This position is required to lead/contribute to the development and implementation of awarding guidelines and policies and procedures and serves as the primary subject matter expert and loan knowledge resource for the office. In addition to their supporting the office, the position is responsible for the training and supervision of one permanent SHRA employee (Loan and Accounting Senior Financial Aid Counselor). Oversight of the Loan programs is a highly compliance-related position where there is a high likely of a state/federal audit review. Accuracy, expert knowledge of state/federal regulations, problem solving skill, and an aptitude for attention to detail are critical skills in this role.</div> Financial Aid - 10208 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35894 2026-09-04T10:38:17-04:00 2026-09-04T10:38:17-04:00 Classification & Compensation Operations HR Specialist <div>This position serves as a Classification &amp; Compensation Operations Specialist which provides support for compensation, employment, and operational processes within UNC Greensboro. The role supports the administration of position management, compensation actions, pay and leave-related processes, and HR transactional activities while ensuring accuracy, consistency, and compliance with applicable federal and state regulations, UNC System requirements, and University policies. The position also supports data analysis, reporting, testing, and process improvement initiatives to enhance the efficiency and effectiveness of service delivery.<br><br><strong>NOTE: This position is designated as hybrid, requiring a minimum of three (3) days per week of in-person work at the assigned Greensboro office location.</strong></div> Human Resources - 58401 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/32254 2025-06-05T09:50:23-04:00 2025-06-05T09:50:24-04:00 Athletic Trainer Certified (ATC) - Part Time <div>The Athletic Trainer is the primary responder responsible for providing care for routine and emergent injuries sustained during Club Sports events. Playing a vital role in the department’s emergency action plan, AT’s work with the Competitive Sports Staff to ensure club participants, spectators and visitors are afforded a reasonably safe participation environment. <br><br><strong>Task &amp; Supervision</strong></div><div>AT’s report directly to the Assistant Director of Competitive Sports and may receive additional direction from all members of the Competitive Sports Leadership Team (Competitive Sports Coordinator and Graduate Assistant/Intern) and the supervising physician. These staff members respond to emergencies providing efficient and immediate care to the critically ill and injured abiding by the department’s emergency action plan. In addition, AT’s are responsible for treating minor injuries.</div><div>In addition to providing immediate care, AT’s are responsible for determining a participant’s fitness for returning to play including evaluating the potential for sustained concussions. AT’s should monitor environmental factors that may impact participant and spectator safety. In the event of the need to deny participation or modify a play schedule, these staff must exhibit strong leadership and communication to ensure potential risks are mitigated.</div><div>AT’s daily responsibilities include, but are not limited to, the follow:</div><div><strong>Event Coverage (85%)</strong></div><ul><li>Provide onsite care and management of injuries including prevention, evaluation, and treatment</li><li>Provide emergency medical care for conditions including, but not limited to: cardiac arrest, commotio cordis, cervical spine injury, traumatic brain injury, heat stroke and exertional sickling</li><li>Monitor and assess environmental factors that may impact safety of participants</li><li>Communicate with players, coaches, and staff regarding the injury status of participants</li><li>Provide rehabilitation, treatment, and referral recommendations as necessary</li></ul><div><strong>Communication &amp; Record Keeping (15%)</strong></div><ul><li>Complete all required documentation regarding injury care</li><li>Communicate with supervising physician regarding issues related to care and appropriate practices</li><li>Monitor medical supply inventory levels and communicate replacement needs</li><li>Assist in the development of the care protocols in conjunction with the supervising physician</li></ul><div><br></div><div><strong>Position will begin early August 2025. Hours vary based on sport club competitions.</strong></div> Recreation and Wellness - 44801 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35849 2026-08-31T13:37:57-04:00 2026-08-31T13:37:57-04:00 Administrative Support Specialist <div>The Department of Human Resources is seeking qualified individuals for temporary Administrative Support Specialist positions that MAY become available on campus. <br><br><strong>When a UNCG Department is in need of a temporary Administrative Support Specialist, qualified applicants who have applied to this temporary pool will be considered.<br><br></strong>Duties and responsibilities could include but are not limited to the following: Banner Processing, Office Management, Departmental HR functions, Assisting with/or Managing Departmental Budget, Providing professional support and customer service to clients, students, Faculty, and/or Staff, Assisting with clerical and administrative duties, Processing travel arrangements and reimbursements, Composing written materials; including memos, emails, agendas or minutes from meetings, and Other duties assigned by Supervisor.</div> Human Resources - 58401 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35503 2026-07-24T11:46:15-04:00 2026-07-24T11:46:16-04:00 Administrative Support Associate <div><br>This part-time <strong>Admin Support Associate</strong> position will be housed in one of the Bryan School’s six academic departments, the<strong> Department of Information Systems and Supply Chain Management</strong>. Reporting to the department head, this position works closely with the department’s lead administrative staff. Work assignments may vary and are primarily customer-oriented and administrative in nature.<br><br></div><div>Responsibilities include customer service, academic program support, clerical responsibilities, and business operations support. Activities may include other duties, as assigned by supervisor.<br><br></div> Info Sys and Supply Chn Mngmt - 11806 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35749 2026-08-20T08:42:32-04:00 2026-08-20T08:42:33-04:00 EUC Technical Services Coordinator <div>The EUC Technical Services Coordinator reports to ITS and serves as a frontline technical resource providing audiovisual, presentation technology, and instructional technology support across Elliott University Center spaces and campus classrooms. This position ensures that technology systems in meeting rooms, conference spaces, and event venues are operational, well-maintained, and ready to support the diverse needs of the campus community.</div><div><br>The position works with student organizations, university departments, faculty, and external clients to assess technology needs and resolve issues related to presentation equipment, hybrid meeting systems, and classroom technology. Responsibilities include supporting audiovisual systems, providing guidance to building users, and assisting with events and scheduled programs.</div><div><br></div><div>This position collaborates with other members of the Classroom Technology team and the Technical Services team and campus partners to coordinate daily technology support and contribute to maintaining consistent, high-quality audiovisual and instructional technology services throughout the Elliott University Center.</div> Info Technology Services - 23101 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35303 2026-06-30T10:39:27-04:00 2026-06-30T10:39:28-04:00 Program Specialist <div>The primary purpose of the Program Specialist position is to provide technical assistance and capacity building services to multiple SERVE Center clients, including state education agencies, government entities, and community-based organizations supporting Out-of-School Time programs. The Program Specialist delivers research- and policy-informed guidance to strengthen program design, ensure alignment with federal and state requirements, support effective implementation, and student outcomes. Responsibilities include strategic planning, development of tools and professional learning, and support for compliance, monitoring, and continuous improvement efforts<br><br>Additionally, this position will lead and support client capacity building efforts related to other SERVE grants such as the Region 5 Comprehensive Center as well as support SERVE’s non-profit contract evaluation efforts.</div> SERVE - 12004 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35899 2026-09-04T12:51:43-04:00 2026-09-04T12:51:43-04:00 Assistant Director of Evaluation <div>The CYFCP Assistant Director of Evaluation provides leadership for evaluation and applied research activities across CYFCP programs. This role leads day-to-day evaluation operations for assigned initiatives, strengthens evaluation infrastructure and quality assurance processes, and provides evaluation consultation and technical assistance to program teams. The Assistant Director of Evaluation directly supervises evaluation personnel, including Research Assistants, Graduate Assistants, and other evaluation support roles as assigned, and ensures evaluation deliverables are completed with accuracy, consistency, and timeliness to meet CYFCP and funder expectations.</div> Center-Youth-Families & Comm - 11504 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/33021 2025-10-09T14:35:08-04:00 2025-10-09T14:35:09-04:00 Family Training Coordinator <div>The Family Training Coordinator will provide leadership and coordination for the training, credentialing, and technical assistance offerings within the Family and Youth Support and Education Program. The types of peer training that will be offered include both formal and informal training opportunities that will be interactive and use best practices in adult education for both in-person and online training opportunities. The Family Training Coordinator will work with their program team members to develop the trainings and certifications, and the trainings and certifications developed by the program staff for local and State partners will be in line with national certification and training standards (e.g., the National Federation of Families’ National Family Peer Specialist Certification).</div> Center-Youth-Families & Comm - 11504 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35851 2026-08-31T14:07:39-04:00 2026-08-31T14:07:40-04:00 Plumber <div>The primary purpose of this position is the maintenance and repair of campus plumbing systems, from the city water supply to the sewage systems. Included in this is the installation and repair of the plumbing fixtures and planned and preventative maintenance on existing water and sewage disposal systems. This position reports to the Plumbing Shop supervisor and is responsible for the maintenance of domestic water, heating equipment, and other routine maintenance as assigned by supervision.<br><br>This position is a mandatory position as defined in the Adverse Weather and Emergency Event Policy.</div> Utility Operations - 56406 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35577 2026-07-31T00:00:48-04:00 2026-07-31T00:00:50-04:00 Graduate Program Advisor <div>The <strong>Graduate Academic Advisor</strong> position is a permanent position that will report to the Administrative Director of Graduate Programs in the Bryan School of Business and Economics. The primary areas of responsibility will be to serve as a Graduate Program Advisor and contribute to improved retention, time‑to‑degree, and student satisfaction outcomes for students in the MBA Program and its affiliated certificates.<br><br></div><ul><li>Manage advising caseload reflective of current MBA enrollments</li><li>Manage online student engagement</li><li>Manage professional development programming</li><li>Participate in recruitment activities and advise prospective students interested in the Accelerated Masters Program and the Dual Registration track</li><li>Serve as chapter advisor for Beta Gamma Sigma honor society, and Spartan Women in Business</li><li>Manage study abroad programming and course (MBA 745) planning</li><li>Plan events like Beta Gamma Sigma ceremony, Graduation networking celebrations etc. Support orientation events</li><li>Support Graduate Programs Office Operations</li><li>Other duties as assigned</li></ul><div><br>Employee attributes needed for success in this role:</div><ul><li>Ability to multi-task and balance multiple priorities or projects in a fast-paced work environment</li><li>Willingness to embrace innovative advising practices using technologies.</li><li>Demonstrated ability to participate in a team environment and to make a positive contribution toward the mission and vision of the organization.</li><li>Adept at interacting with others in a professional and collaborative manner.</li><li>Excellent leadership skills and ability to manage sizeable projects, delegating when appropriate.</li><li>Strong organizational skills and attention to detail.</li><li>Excellent oral and written communication skills.</li></ul><div><br></div> MBA Office - 11808 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35902 2026-09-04T14:15:22-04:00 2026-09-04T14:15:22-04:00 Director of Financial Planning and Budgets <div>The Director of Financial Planning and Budgets<strong> </strong>provides strategic leadership for the university’s comprehensive budget development, financial planning, and analytical functions. This role oversees the direction, administration, and continuous improvement of complex budget processes, ensuring alignment with institutional priorities and full compliance with university, state, and federal requirements. Serving as a key advisor to senior leadership, the Director leads a team responsible for developing reports, interpreting financial data, modeling scenarios, projecting revenues and expenditures, and identifying trends that inform strategic decision‑making.<br><br></div><div>The position maintains direct communication with the Office of State Budget and Management (OSBM), the UNC System Office (UNCSO), and campus leaders including Vice Chancellors, Deans, Department Heads, and Directors. The Director establishes and maintains effective budget procedures, prepares high‑level analyses and presentations for executive leadership, evaluates financial options, and reports on outcomes of budgetary decisions. Core functional responsibilities include team building, customer service, managerial oversight, reporting, planning and projections, reversion planning, coordination of carryforwards and special allocations, debt‑related issues, campus training, all other general budget matters, and addressing special requests. Professionalism, collaboration, and sound judgment are essential to success in this role.</div> Fin Planning and Budgets - 56203 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35787 2026-08-21T08:52:25-04:00 2026-08-21T08:52:26-04:00 Second Shift Parking Operations Lead <div>The position requires an individual who is energetic and customer service-oriented, with the ability to multi-task and process payments at the cashier window of the Walker Parking Deck. The position will monitor CCTV security system and act as dispatch for parking enforcement personnel. This position will also provide intercom/phone-based customer service and operate multiple parking management systems. This position oversees student employees to ensure necessary work is completed and reporting any issues with student employees. Will provide on call coverage on a rotating monthly basis to ensure coverage for deck operations and handle any issues that may arise during the weekend shifts.</div> Parking Services - 57701 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35311 2026-07-01T00:01:11-04:00 2026-07-01T00:01:12-04:00 Administrative Support Associate <div>The University of North Carolina at Greensboro is a public, coeducational, doctoral-granting, residential university chartered in 1891. It is one of the three original institutions of The University of North Carolina System. <br><strong>The Department of Human Resources is seeking qualified individuals for temporary Administrative Support Associate positions that may become available on campus. <br></strong><br>When a UNCG Department is in need of a temporary Administrative Support Associate, qualified applicants who have applied to this temporary pool will be considered.<br><br>Duties and responsibilities could include, but are not limited to the following:</div><ul><li>Providing professional support and customer service to clients, students, Faculty, and/or Staff</li><li>Assisting the with clerical and administrative duties</li><li>Answering and transferring telephone calls</li><li>Composing written materials; including memos, emails, agendas, or minutes from meetings</li><li>Banner Processing</li><li>Ordering office supplies</li><li>Other duties assigned by Supervisor</li></ul> Human Resources - 58401 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/34136 2026-02-09T09:08:22-05:00 2026-02-09T09:08:23-05:00 Open Rank Faculty Position in Kinesiology <div>We are seeking an innovative scholar in Kinesiology with interest and experience in graduate education to take a major role in our Doctor of Education (EdD) in Kinesiology program. The EdD in KIN is an online cohort-based, interdisciplinary degree program tailored to meet the needs of professionals in kinesiology. Our EdD students work in varied areas across kinesiology bringing professional skills and expertise to the forefront of their work. Their dissertation projects are designed to have real impact in their professional practice or community; translation of their findings into action is a key to a successful dissertation. The successful candidate will demonstrate the ability to balance a strong teaching and research portfolio with a commitment to supporting active kinesiology professionals in the field. More information on the program can be found at: <br><a href=\"https://kin.uncg.edu/graduate-degrees/doctor-of-education-online/\"><strong>https://kin.uncg.edu/graduate-degrees/doctor-of-education-online/ </strong></a><br><br></div><div>Primary responsibilities include teaching, advising, and supervision of dissertations in the EdD program, maintaining an active line of research, and engaging in departmental, professional, and university service activities. The successful candidate is expected to work with the program director to continue to foster a sense of community within the EdD program and facilitate the dissertation process – a major component of this position. Further, all core faculty members of the EdD program are expected to be actively engaged with department activities and to participate in all virtual and in-person EdD activities.<br><br></div> Kinesiology - 13003 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35853 2026-08-31T14:44:36-04:00 2026-08-31T14:44:37-04:00 Building and Environmental Technician <div>The position is responsible for general and detail cleaning in academic, administrative, and performance buildings on campus. This position also completes floor care, has good customer service skills, and completes other special projects such as furniture supply moves within the academic buildings on campus. Supervisor may assign other job-related duties not specifically listed under essential tasks.<br><br>General and Detail Cleaning – 60%<br>Customer Service – 10%<br>Floor Care – 15%<br>Special Projects – 15%<br><br>This position is a mandatory position as defined in the Adverse Weather and Emergency Event Policy.</div> Facility Services Housekeeping - 56408 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35593 2026-08-01T00:02:24-04:00 2026-08-01T00:02:26-04:00 Assistant/Associate Professor <div>Faculty in the Department of Counseling and Educational Development (CED) in the School of Education at The University of North Carolina at Greensboro seek a colleague for a tenure line Assistant/Associate Professor with a Clinical Mental Health or Couple and Family specialization, with a particular emphasis on addictions. We are searching for a team-oriented individual who would contribute to teaching in our master’s and doctoral programs, and provide leadership and coordination for our Addictions Treatment Post-Baccalaureate Certificate.</div><div><br>This position involves:</div><ul><li>Teaching, supervising, and mentoring students.</li><li>Developing a strong, focused research agenda and pursuing external funding.</li><li>Coordination and outreach activities.</li><li>Program development.</li></ul><div><br>CED is home for graduate students with a variety of racial, socioeconomic, geographical, and cultural backgrounds. CED faculty actively mentor and advise students at both the master’s and doctoral levels. This position is a 9-month full-time position <strong>beginning</strong> <strong>August 1, 2027</strong>.</div> Counseling and Edu Development - 12003 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35313 2026-07-01T00:01:15-04:00 2026-07-01T00:01:17-04:00 Temp Pool Tech Support Technician <div>The Department of Human Resources is seeking qualified individuals to consider for temporary Tech Support Technician positions that MAY become available on campus. <br><strong>When a UNCG Department is in need of a temporary Tech Support Technician, qualified applicants who have applied to this currently active temporary pool will be considered. <br></strong><br>Duties and Responsibilities could include, but are not limited to the following:<br>Personal desktop and device support; Software updates; System Maintenance; Communication and Information; Website Maintenance and Development Other duties assigned by a Supervisor</div> Human Resources - 58401 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35905 2026-09-04T15:30:14-04:00 2026-09-04T15:30:15-04:00 Building and Environmental Technician <div>The position is responsible for general and detail cleaning in academic, administrative, and performance buildings on campus. This position also completes floor care, has good customer service skills, and completes other special projects, such as furniture supply moves within the academic buildings on campus. Supervisor may assign other job-related duties not specifically listed under essential tasks.<br><br>General and Detail Cleaning – 60%<br>Floor Care – 15%<br>Special Projects – 15%<br>Customer Service – 10%<br><br>This position is a mandatory position as defined in the Adverse Weather and Emergency Event Policy.</div> Facility Services Housekeeping - 56408 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35794 2026-08-21T09:53:28-04:00 2026-08-21T09:53:29-04:00 Unit Hardware/Software Support Analyst <div>The primary purpose of this position is to provide technology support services to faculty and staff within the Bryan School and School of Education at UNCG. This position also supports the daily operations of the Campus-Wide Hardware Procurement program as part of the Hardware &amp; Software Support team. Responsibilities include providing analytical and technical assistance, supporting the deployment, maintenance, and lifecycle management of enterprise workstations and peripherals, and resolving issues related to enterprise applications and services to ensure reliable, standards-based technology support across the University. <br><strong><br></strong>Department-specific duties may include:<br><br></div><ul><li><strong>Endpoint Support:</strong><ul><li>Provide desktop and laptop support for faculty, graduate students, and undergraduate student workers’ assigned UNCG-owned devices.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Application Management:</strong><ul><li>Install, maintain, and support unit-specific applications used by faculty and staff, provide training as needed.</li><li>Develop and maintain internal documentation for supported systems, including non-routine procedures, workarounds, and solutions.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Research and Planning</strong><ul><li>Collaborate with ITS Engineering, Security, Networking, CHiP, and Application Management teams to ensure adherence to ITS infrastructure on the below research and planning activities.</li><li>Review, analyze, and evaluate existing systems to identify opportunities for improvement and provide recommendations.</li><li>Support leadership in planning for new products and technologies, including researching emerging technologies related to support systems.</li><li>Investigate potential hardware integration issues within UNCG systems and networks.</li><li>Help define technical requirements for supported systems and provide input to leadership for planning and decision-making.</li></ul></li></ul> Info Technology Services - 23101 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/34503 2026-03-24T14:04:07-04:00 2026-03-24T14:04:08-04:00 Academic Professional Assistant/Associate Professor Physical Activity Instructional Program Coordinator for the Department of Kinesiology <div>We are seeking an Academic Professional Track Assistant/Associate Professor to serve as the Physical Activity Instructional Program Coordinator for the Department of Kinesiology. This is a 9-month appointment with the potential to teach summer classes. The Academic Professional Track offers non-tenured rankings of Assistant Professor through Professor, with an emphasis on teaching and other professional responsibilities. Appointments are renewable.<br><br></div><div>We are seeking a colleague to facilitate and coordinate the physical activity instruction program within the Department of Kinesiology and across the UNCG campus. Typical duties include:<br><br></div><ul><li>Teaching departmental courses (e.g., Strength Training and Conditioning, Lifetime Wellness, Physical Activity Instruction, Exercise Prescription) and physical activity courses.</li><li>Coordination of the physical activity instructional program (e.g., scheduling, equipment management).</li><li>Onboarding, training, and supervision of roughly 12-15 graduate assistants teaching physical activity courses in the department at the beginning of the fall semester.</li><li>Advising undergraduate students with semester course selections and planning their path to graduation.</li><li>Engagement in departmental, university, and community service is expected. In particular, the candidate is expected to develop strong working relationships with other physical activity-related entities across the University (e.g., athletics, campus recreation, student and employee wellness programs).</li></ul><div><br></div> Kinesiology - 13003 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35855 2026-08-31T14:56:23-04:00 2026-08-31T14:56:24-04:00 Assistant Director, Building and Environmental Services <div>The Assistant Director of Building and Environmental Services provides leadership and coordination of housekeeping and custodial services across campus facilities, most often within Housing and Residence Life or Facilities Operations.<br>This position supervises subordinate housekeeping supervisors, delivery personnel, set-up crews, floor maintenance assistants, and housekeeping staff to ensure clean, safe, and well-maintained living and learning environments.<br>Managers in this band are responsible for planning, scheduling, and inspecting housekeeping operations; managing equipment and supplies; ensuring compliance with safety and health standards; and aligning housekeeping activities with the University’s operational goals. The role also requires leadership in employee development, performance management, and customer service, with accountability for both daily operations and long-range planning of custodial programs.<br><br></div><ul><li>30% — Leadership &amp; Housekeeping Operations</li><li>20% — Maintenance &amp; Special Projects</li><li>15% — Customer Service &amp; Stakeholder Engagement</li><li>15% — Contract &amp; Budget Management</li><li>10% — Inventory &amp; MRO Stores Oversight</li><li>5% — Training &amp; Employee Development</li><li>5% — Safety &amp; Compliance</li></ul><div><br>This position is a mandatory position as defined in the Adverse Weather and Emergency Event Policy.</div><div><br></div> Facilities Operations - 56404 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35628 2026-08-06T12:09:39-04:00 2026-08-06T12:09:40-04:00 Academic Records Specialist <div>Reporting to the Assistant Registrar, the Academic Records Specialist is responsible for degree clearance support; tracking of degree progress, certification of graduation for undergraduate students; and serves as a point of contact for the degree clearance area. This position communicates with students, advisors, and other faculty and staff to ensure that graduation applicants have met the requirements for their degrees. This position also assists students needing notarization of documents for the purpose of obtaining an apostille and serves as a backup for ordering diplomas. Additionally, this position will collaborate with the Degree Works team to process curriculum modifications and input foreign language placement test scores and waivers for students.&nbsp;<br><br>This position works collaboratively with Admissions and Transfer Articulation and is responsible for the daily management of the processes associated with Degree Works and graduation clearance for students. This position is responsible for maintaining current knowledge of academic courses, program requirements, and University Catalog policies at UNC Greensboro. The Academic Records Specialist works with others to implement institutional strategic initiatives and ensure compliance with statewide policies and initiatives. This position will work closely with faculty and academic affairs staff to develop proficiency in college academic requirements and to support strategic measures with the UNC System.</div> University Registrar's Office - 10204 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35347 2026-07-07T18:21:51-04:00 2026-07-07T18:21:52-04:00 Assistant/Associate/Full Professor <div><strong>Re-Post, Previous Applicants Need Not Re-Apply, Still Under Consideration</strong><br><br>The School of Nursing at the University of North Carolina at Greensboro is seeking faculty members to apply for a full-time tenure/tenure-track position. The School is recruiting creative and highly motivated candidates who want to advance their academic careers and support the research, teaching, and service mission of the UNCG School of Nursing. We are seeking innovative and talented individuals actively engaged in research and education to become part of our dynamic team. Our research priorities include a focus on vulnerable populations in the areas of chronic disease prevention and management, health disparities, and interventions and symptom management. We are also interested in health services researchers. Other research foci will be considered. <br><br>Tenure/tenure-track positions are research-intensive. Tenure/tenure-track faculty are expected to teach students, pursue a program of research, seek external funding, and disseminate research findings. All positions will have responsibilities in our research, teaching, and service missions. Candidates with experience in these areas are preferred. Candidates must hold or anticipate a research doctoral degree in nursing or related fields by <strong>start date</strong>. Tenure is available at the Associate Professor or full Professor ranks for those who meet the criteria.<br><br></div><div>This is a 9-month academic year position with benefits.<br><br><strong>There are 3 openings for this posting.</strong></div> Nursing - 12802 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35799 2026-08-21T10:19:34-04:00 2026-08-21T10:19:35-04:00 Unit Hardware/Software Support Analyst <div>The primary purpose of this position is to provide technology support services to faculty and staff within the University Libraries at UNCG. As part of the Embedded Endpoint Support team, this position also supports the daily operations of the Campus-Wide Hardware Procurement program. Responsibilities include providing analytical and technical assistance, supporting the deployment, maintenance, and lifecycle management of enterprise workstations and peripherals, and resolving issues related to enterprise applications and services to ensure reliable, standards-based technology support across the University. <br><strong><br></strong>Department-specific duties may include:<strong> </strong><br><br></div><ul><li><strong>Website Content Management</strong>:<ul><li>In conjunction with the library website administrator, create, update, and evaluate website pages and posts as needed to ensure that web content is current, accurate, and accessible; monitor website comments and questions and respond directly or forwards them for action, as appropriate; review weekly accessibility and search engine optimization reports for needed corrections; complete the annual website content audit.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Application Software and Hardware Support</strong>:<ul><li>Develop and maintain documentation providing practices and solutions for applications and software used by clients in the University Libraries; may be intended for both internal use and end users as appropriate.</li><li>Support the tools needed for access to University Libraries’ hosted applications and the necessary data transfer protocols.</li><li>Install, configure, and support library-specific hardware devices and peripherals, including self-check units, barcode/magstripe readers, and receipt/label printers.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Research and Planning</strong>:<ul><li>Collaborate with ITS Engineering, Security, Networking, CHiP, and Application Management teams to ensure adherence to ITS infrastructure on the below research and planning activities.</li><li>Research and identify appropriate technologies for Library computing environment projects, conduct a cost analysis, define the scope of work, and assess project timelines as needed.</li><li>Research, implement, and assist clients with new applications related to Library-specific end-user need.</li></ul></li></ul><div><br><br></div> Info Technology Services - 23101 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/34734 2026-04-21T14:37:17-04:00 2026-04-21T14:37:18-04:00 Nurse Practitioner Faculty <div>The School of Nursing at the University of North Carolina Greensboro (UNCG) is seeking a dual certified Psychiatric-Mental Health Nurse Practitioner (PMHNP) and Family Nurse Practitioner (FNP) or Adult-Gerontology Primary Care Nurse Practitioner (AGPCNP). Dual certification is strongly preferred; however, we will also consider candidates who hold either a PMHNP or an FNP/AGPCNP certification. The position is for a Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor, or Clinical Professor. We are looking for creative, innovative, and highly motivated candidates who want to support the teaching, scholarship, and service mission of the UNCG School of Nursing and advance their academic careers. Ideal candidates will have current specialty certification, teaching, and current clinical experience, and a background in evidence-based practice. Candidates must hold a master's degree in nursing. An unencumbered RN license in North Carolina and a current certification as a NP is required prior to the employment date. Salary and rank will be commensurate with experience and credentials. For more information about the school, please visit our website at <a href=\"https://nursing.uncg.edu/\"><strong>https://nursing.uncg.edu</strong></a>.</div> Nursing - 12802 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35857 2026-09-01T10:44:20-04:00 2026-09-01T10:44:20-04:00 HR Business Partner <div>The Human Resources Business Partners collaborate with client groups and HR teams to develop and deliver effective human capital programs and policies and practices that align with business objectives, drive superior business results and contribute to the overall efficiency and effectiveness of the organization. The position will focus primarily on the areas of people strategy and organizational effectiveness, change leadership and coaching, management level employee relations support and conflict resolution.<br><br></div><div>The position performs Human Resource program management functions for its’ respective divisional function(s) as well as serving as the expert in employee relations campus-wide. This position formulates partnerships across the HR function to deliver value-added service to management.<br><br><strong>NOTE: This position is designated as hybrid, requiring a minimum of three (3) days per week of in-person work at the assigned Greensboro office location.</strong></div> Human Resources - 58401 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35640 2026-08-10T08:50:33-04:00 2026-08-10T08:50:35-04:00 Salesforce Application Administrator <div>This position serves as the institutional Application Administrator and IT System Administrator for University Advancement’s Kindsight Ascend CRM, built on Salesforce. The role partners closely with Advancement Operations, frontline fundraisers, and campus stakeholders to translate fundraising and engagement needs into scalable, secure, and well-governed CRM functionality.<br><br>System administrators exercise independent technical authority while following institutional and regulatory standards. This position is accountable for lifecycle management, technical enablement, system availability, security, access management, configuration, data integrity, integrations, and compliance for applications with division-wide and institution-wide impact. Failures or security issues associated with the systems administered by this role may escalate to executive IT leadership (CIO/CISO), making this position accountable for audit findings, continuity of operations, and risk mitigation.<br><br></div><div>This position owns privileged access and security design for enterprise applications assigned to it, including user roles, administrative permissions, and access reviews in alignment with institutional audit and compliance requirements. This position is accountable for protecting sensitive data through appropriate access controls, configuration management, and vendor security coordination. This position ensures that system configurations, upgrades, and integrations adhere to University standards and do not introduce audit risk, data exposure, or compliance failures (e.g., FERPA, HIPAA, SOX, PCI, or other applicable regulations).<br><br></div><div>This position maintains operational continuity and availability of enterprise systems by proactively managing system performance, capacity, and user-impacting behaviors. This role plans upgrades and designs integrations, evaluating vendor releases, patches, and roadmap changes to ensure availability and stability for all users, and serves as the primary escalation point for production incidents and system failures, coordinating response activities with vendors, infrastructure teams, and integration partners. This position ensures coverage is in place to mitigate institutional risk during staff absences or turnover by providing cross-training and system and process documentation. This role also supports continuous improvement efforts across the systems it administers.<br><br></div> Info Technology Services - 23101 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35422 2026-07-14T16:05:45-04:00 2026-07-14T16:05:46-04:00 Assistant Director of New Student Transitions <div>The Assistant Director will have direct oversight of Your First Year (YFY) program development, marketing, execution, and assessment. This role manages departmental marketing and communications, and provides logistical support for Spartan Orientation Advising and Registration (SOAR), ONL100 &amp; 101, NAV1GATE (the Chancellor’s New Student Convocation), and similar initiatives and other key first-year engagement events.<br><br></div><div>The Assistant Director supervises two graduate students and several undergraduate students in support of Your First Year and departmental marketing efforts. Additionally, this position oversees the creative content team, offering input and guidance on best practices for marketing and communications, and coordinates volunteer groups.<br><br></div><div>This role represents the department at university events, such as SOAR and Admissions events, and serves on various campus-wide committees, including University Pro Comms and Rawkin’ Welcome Weeks. The position is also responsible for managing several funds and evaluating programs for student impact, return on investment (ROI), and improvement planning.<br><br></div><div>The Assistant Director reports to the Associate Director of New Student Transitions within the New Student Transitions and First Year Experience department.</div> New Student Transition and FYE - 44601 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/25110 2023-01-30T10:51:17-05:00 2023-01-30T10:51:17-05:00 Early Childhood Teacher Assistant/Floater and Substitute <div>The Teacher Assistant works in early education classrooms serving children between the ages of 0-5. This person may float from room to room as needed for support. This person assists the teacher with caregiving routines, activities, supervising groups of children indoors and outdoors as well as light housekeeping duties such as serving or cleaning after meals.</div> Human Devlp and Family Studies - 12403 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35825 2026-08-26T15:33:40-04:00 2026-08-26T15:33:41-04:00 Business Officer <div>The Business Officer is a member of the CYFCP leadership team. The Business Officer will manage the day-to-day operations of a robust center with 10 active areas of expertise encompassing 63 staff and total externally funded grants in excess of 13 million. This position will serve in a pre-and post-award capacity, develop and manage complex budgets related to the operations of the center as well as the external grants, participate in strategic planning of the center to continue its growth and expansion into other areas of expertise, and handle talent management for the center.</div> Center-Youth-Families & Comm - 11504 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35680 2026-08-12T12:37:11-04:00 2026-08-12T12:37:12-04:00 Academic Recovery Coordinator <div>Reporting to the Associate Director of Academic Recovery, the Academic Recovery Coordinator will collaborate with other members of the AR Team to coordinate, implement, and assess ARS 100 and 120, the academic recovery interventions for new students who fall on Academic Probation and Academic Suspension. The ARC serves as the academic coach for an assigned load of ARS 100 and ARS 120 students. In addition, the ARC supports SFO’s one-stop-shop services by . providing supplemental academic advising assistance during SFO’s drop-in hours and via scheduled student appointments.<br><br>More detailed information is listed under “Key Responsibilities” below.<br>Other relevant duties as assigned; some evening and weekend work required.</div> Students First Office - 10918 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/34968 2026-05-22T00:00:39-04:00 2026-05-22T00:00:42-04:00 Assistant Director for Compliance <div>The Assistant Director will assist the Assistant Athletic Director for Compliance in the day-to-day operations of the Athletics Compliance Office including assisting with compliance rules education programs for coaches, staff, student-athletes, and external groups to ensure appropriate people are knowledgeable of and comply with pertinent NCAA and Southern Conference standards; assisting in the preparation of NCAA required reporting (APR and GSR), assisting with interpretive questions, NCAA waivers (PTD, legislative, etc.) as appropriate; and conducting internal monitoring and auditing programs that adapt with continuously changing regulations. This position is also responsible for assisting with the hiring and supervising of compliance office student-workers and interns. This individual is responsible for following the policies and procedures of the University, Conference and the NCAA in day-to-day operation of the program.</div> Intercollegiate Athletics - 85001 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35871 2026-09-02T08:10:22-04:00 2026-09-02T08:10:23-04:00 Physical Chemistry - Assistant Professor- Tenure Track <div>The Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry at the University of North Carolina at Greensboro is seeking to fill a tenure-track faculty position in the area of Physical Chemistry at the rank of Assistant Professor with an anticipated start date of August 2027. Research interests that tie directly into UNCG priorities of Energy, AI/New Technology, and/or Health/Medicine will be greatly preferred. A PhD in Chemistry, Physical Chemistry, or a related field is a requirement for the position. Applicants should demonstrate a solid record of accomplishment in publications and should show promise for establishing an independent and externally funded research program. Applicants will be expected to mentor master’s and doctoral research students, and to contribute to the department’s long-standing strength in undergraduate research. Additionally, the successful hire will demonstrate teaching excellence at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. A competitive start up package will be provided.<br><br>Applications must be submitted through Spartan Talent. To apply, visit https://jobsearch.uncg.edu and click on “Faculty/Tenure Stream and apply to position 1096 Applicants should upload a cover letter addressed to Dr. Liam Duffy, Committee Chair, a curriculum vita (CV), a description of proposed research, a teaching statement and identify at least three (3) contacts who will send a letter of recommendation. Any technical questions concerning the application submission process can be addressed to Trina Porcher at t_porche@uncg.edu. Review of application will begin 10/01/2026 and will continue until the position is filled.<br><br>UNCG is a Minority Serving Institution. UNCG and the Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry foster an environment of collaboration across departments and schools and support community-engaged research. UNCG is located in Greensboro, the largest city in North Carolina’s Piedmont Triad region and the third-most populous city in the state. Greensboro is a vibrant city with nearly 300,000 residents and more than 47,000 college students and is known for its expansive parks and greenway system, arts, music, and sports.<br><br></div> Chemistry & Biochemistry - 12205 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35431 2026-07-15T16:49:52-04:00 2026-07-15T16:49:53-04:00 Assistant Professors of Management or Marketing <div>The Bryan School of Business and Economics is seeking qualified applicants for two tenure-stream positions at the rank of <strong>Assistant Professor </strong>(tenure-track) in the Department of Management and/or the Department of Marketing, Entrepreneurship, Hospitality and Tourism, beginning August 1, 2027. The positions can be in the areas of Management, Marketing, Innovation, or Strategy, but the central expectation is a focus on the <strong>use of Artificial Intelligence in both their instruction and research</strong>.<br><br>While these are discipline-specific faculty positions, successful candidates are expected to demonstrate the capacity to integrate artificial intelligence meaningfully into their teaching and research. The School is especially interested in candidates whose expertise will strengthen departmental teaching and research needs while also contributing to the Bryan School’s broader capacity to prepare students and faculty to understand, evaluate, and use AI tools responsibly and effectively. Once established, these faculty are expected to serve as a resource to enable other faculty to increase the infusion of artificial intelligence in the curriculum.<br><br></div><div>The University emphasizes high-quality in research and teaching, and teaching responsibilities will primarily be at the undergraduate level and will include both online and face-to-face instruction. Service to the University and to the academic and/or practicing professions is also expected.</div><div><br></div> Dean's Office - BE - 11801 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/27400 2023-09-27T15:57:29-04:00 2023-09-27T15:57:30-04:00 Bilingual Research Assistants (English/Spanish) <ul><li>Assist with the administration of language assessments to Latino preschool children (training provided) at preschools in the Greensboro and High Point areas.</li><li>Assist with data entry</li></ul> Comm Sciences and Disorders - 13001 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35832 2026-08-28T14:19:40-04:00 2026-08-28T14:19:41-04:00 Clinical Psychology Assistant Professor <div>The Department of Psychology at the University of North Carolina at Greensboro invites applications for a tenure-track position in Clinical Psychology (Assistant Professor level) to begin August 1, 2027.<br><br></div><div>We seek someone to join an active and collaborative department. The Department of Psychology consists of 28 full-time faculty and offers a BA and BS in psychology, including Disciplinary Honors, an MA in experimental psychology, and a PhD in clinical, cognitive, developmental, and social psychology (see <a href=\"https://psy.uncg.edu/\"><strong>https://psy.uncg.edu/</strong></a> for more information).<br><br></div><div>The doctoral program in Clinical Psychology is accredited by the American Psychological Association. UNCG’s clinical program emphasizes the integration of science and practice, values both basic and applied research on human behavior across the life span and encourages collaboration across research areas. We have ongoing research expertise in early childhood development, parenting, trauma, life stress, depression, couples, and adolescent and emerging adult psychopathology. Our department is home to the UNCG Psychology Clinic (https://psy.uncg.edu/clinic/), our doctoral training clinic that provides mental health services to the broader community, with a focus on providing empirically supported treatments to underserved populations in a culturally competent manner.</div> Psychology - 12215 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35696 2026-08-14T15:48:49-04:00 2026-08-14T15:48:50-04:00 Director of Enrollment Communications <div>The Director, Office of Enrollment Communications, will serve as the primary strategic leader for the University’s enrollment marketing efforts. The director will closely collaborate with leadership in the Division of Enrollment Management, The Graduate School, the Division of Student Success, University Communications, and various academic units to develop data-driven marketing strategies that increase enrollment (on-campus and online) and improve student experience. This individual is responsible for identifying and understanding marketing needs and leading the planning and executing of multiple, complex integrated campaigns that will drive University enrollment. Specific responsibilities include:</div><ul><li>Annual strategic planning for marketing campaigns (collateral/direct mail/advertising) to support undergraduate and graduate student recruitment (on-campus and online), admission communications, new student onboarding, Financial Aid, Registration, and other business processes for enrolled students.</li><li>Website management for multiple entities including Enrollment, Admissions, Graduate School, and Spartan Central (Financial Aid, Registrar, and Cashiers Office).</li><li>Administration and oversight of content creation for communication-related elements of Undergraduate Admissions and Graduate School CRM systems.</li></ul><div><br></div><div>This position will be supported by a team of digital and traditional marketing professionals, including strategic experts, project managers, and a small creative staff (copywriting/design). The director will lead the department staff to work with agility and knowledge, which requires a leader who possesses a breadth of marketing/communications experience and a willingness to roll up their sleeves and do project-level work at times. They should be as savvy at developing new strategies as they are at executing them.</div><div><br></div><div>The ideal individual must have a well-rounded knowledge of integrated marketing communications disciplines and a track record of executing on strategic campaigns that exceed expectations while remaining on time and on budget.</div><div><br></div><div>This individual must demonstrate a commitment to continual learning -- for themselves and their staff members -- to stay on top of industry trends. Expert leadership skills are required and should include presentation skills, budget management, reporting, consulting, supervision, and a track record of staff development. Some project management, copywriting, and basic graphic design skills will be required on occasion. Prior experience managing print projects, especially in a higher-ed setting, is ideal.</div><div><br></div> University Communications - 33901 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35183 2026-06-17T00:00:36-04:00 2026-06-17T00:00:38-04:00 Assistant Clinical Director <div>The Department of Counseling and Educational Development in the School of Education at The University of North Carolina at Greensboro seeks applicants for a part-time, 12-month masters-level counselor for the job of Assistant Director in the departmental Nicholas A. Vacc Counseling and Consulting Clinic (Vacc). The majority of the work will be provided in the Nicholas A Vacc Counseling and Consulting Clinic with some work and tasks occurring at the department level. The person in this position will provide clinical and administrative support within the Vacc Clinic by providing consultation and clinical supervision to counseling students, and by taking the lead on special projects that support the training of students in the Vacc Clinic. Examples include program development, exploring new referral sources on campus and in the greater Greensboro community, developing and fine-tuning Clinic policies and procedures. This position will coordinate record keeping to ensure compliance with ethical and legal standards, provide on-call crisis consultation during the day and/or evening hours, and provide general clinical consultation to counselors-in-training and supervisors-in-training. Additional responsibilities may include managing Clinic staff, collaborating and networking on campus, providing and developing marketing and public relations materials and presentations.<br><br></div><div>We are seeking a colleague with strong clinical skills, a clear counselor identity, administrative and organizational capacity, the ability to support the clinical training of students, and to work independently on a variety of assignments and tasks.</div> Counseling and Edu Development - 12003 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35881 2026-09-02T15:01:21-04:00 2026-09-02T15:01:23-04:00 Fire Alarm Technician <div>**Re-Post, Previous Applicants Need Not Re-Apply, Still Under Consideration<br><br>This is a skilled position with responsibility to operate, maintain, repair, and upgrade, as directed, the automated fire alarm systems on campus. This position also performs hardware and software preventive maintenance, repairs, improvements and participate in an on-call rotation.<br><br>40% – Repair of Fire Alarm Systems<br>40% – Maintenance of Fire Alarm and all Safety Equipment<br>15% – Record Keeping and Administration of All Testing and Inspections of Fire Protection Systems<br>5% – Construction – In-House<br><br>This is a mandatory position as defined in the Adverse Weather and Emergency Event policy. Mandatory employees are expected to report to or remain at work during adverse weather and emergency events and, if deemed necessary, to work a different schedule or shift than normally assigned.</div> Utility Operations - 56406 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35834 2026-08-28T14:37:02-04:00 2026-08-28T14:37:02-04:00 Assistant Professor, Finance <div>The Bryan School of Business and Economics is seeking a qualified applicant for a tenure-stream position at the rank of <strong>Assistant Professor of Finance </strong>(tenure-track) in the Department of Accounting and Finance, beginning August 1, 2027. Candidates from all areas of finance are encouraged to apply; however, the successful candidate is expected to incorporate <strong>artificial intelligence meaningfully into their teaching and research</strong>.<br><br>The School is especially interested in candidates whose expertise will strengthen departmental teaching and research needs while also contributing to the Bryan School’s broader capacity to prepare students and faculty to understand, evaluate, and use AI tools responsibly and effectively. Once established, the faculty is expected to serve as a resource to enable other faculty to increase the infusion of artificial intelligence in the curriculum.<br><br></div><div>The University emphasizes high-quality research and teaching. Teaching responsibilities will include undergraduate and graduate courses delivered both online and in person. Service to the University and the academic and/or professional communities is also expected.</div> Accounting and Finance - 11812 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35459 2026-07-20T09:50:34-04:00 2026-07-20T09:50:36-04:00 Manager of Student Health Access <div>The Manager of Student Health Access provides leadership and oversight for student-facing administrative operations within Student Health Services. This position is responsible for healthcare access services, insurance administration, provider credentialing, revenue cycle support, health information oversight, STAT referral coordination, customer service operations, and administrative support functions. The manager serves as a primary resource for students, staff, providers, and external partners regarding healthcare access, insurance coverage, billing processes, medical records, and operational services while ensuring compliance with university policies, HIPAA regulations, accreditation standards, and healthcare industry best practices. The position supervises administrative support staff and develops processes that support efficient operations and a positive student experience.<br><br></div> Student Health Services - 44604 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/30480 2024-10-28T00:02:22-04:00 2024-10-28T00:02:25-04:00 Post-Doctoral Fellow <div>The Oberlies Research Group in the Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry at the University of North Carolina at Greensboro is seeking a postdoctoral chemist for a suite of projects. All of these require a passion for working with fungi, both in the mycology and chemistry labs. The ideal candidate will have earned a Ph.D. in pharmacognosy, medicinal/organic chemistry, analytical chemistry, and/or natural products chemistry. While the specific skill sets are somewhat flexible, direct experience with how to isolate, measure, and/or determine the structures of secondary metabolites with NMR and/or mass spectrometry is a requirement. In addition, direct experience with the growth and propagation of fungi is highly desirable.</div> Chemistry & Biochemistry - 12205 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35715 2026-08-18T00:00:47-04:00 2026-08-18T00:00:51-04:00 Associate Director for Institutional Research and Enterprise Data Governance <div>The Associate Director of Institutional Research and Enterprise Data Governance provides leadership for the University’s traditional institutional research, external reporting, survey, applied analytics, and enterprise data governance functions. This role oversees the Surveys, Research, and Analytics and Enterprise Data Governance functions within IREDM. The position is responsible for managing state, federal, and external reporting; coordinating major institutional surveys; leading and contributing to applied research and analytical studies; and advancing enterprise data governance practices related to data stewardship, institutional definitions, data quality, data cataloging, governance workflows, and responsible data use.&nbsp;<br><br>In addition to supervising professional staff, the Associate Director serves as a working manager who actively contributes to complex institutional research projects, reporting efforts, survey submissions, analytical studies, and governance initiatives. The position plays a key role in translating institutional data into meaningful insights for campus leadership, academic units, administrative units, and external stakeholders, while also ensuring that institutional data are consistently defined, well-governed, and aligned with University standards. This role collaborates closely with Reporting and Visualization, Data Engineering and Architecture, campus data stewards, and functional data owners to support a coordinated institutional data ecosystem that balances access, usability, compliance, quality, and accountability. This position is eligible for teleworking; however, some in-person assignments may be necessary at the supervisor’s discretion.</div> Inst Research/Entr Data Mgmt - 10803 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35203 2026-06-19T10:22:46-04:00 2026-06-19T10:22:46-04:00 Associate Professor <div>Applicants working broadly in Nanomedicine or Synthetic Biology with a focus on human health and medicine are welcome to apply. This includes areas such as nanomedicine development, smart biomaterial design, biomedical engineering, drug delivery, diagnostic nanotechnology, gene therapy, and the study of nanoparticle interactions with biological systems, including micro physiological systems and tissue engineering. Candidates whose work can complement or further advance the department’s current research efforts, preferably through experimental approaches, are especially encouraged to apply. Qualified applicants will have earned a PhD in any relevant scientific discipline, such as biomedical engineering, bioengineering, molecular biology, pharmacology, or microbiology, and will have at least 2 years of postdoctoral training. Competitive candidates will have an excellent research record, as demonstrated by their publication record, and either exhibit strong prospects for extramural funding or have an established extramural funding record. The new faculty will be expected to develop an externally supported research program, teach effectively at the graduate level, collaborate with researchers in the Joint School of Nanoscience &amp; Nanoengineering as well as with researchers in their field, and participate in Departmental and University service activities, with opportunities at the Joint School to engage in entrepreneurial activities.<br><br></div> Dean's Office - NN - 13201 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35889 2026-09-03T09:51:00-04:00 2026-09-03T09:51:01-04:00 Building and Environmental Technician <div>The position is responsible for general and detail cleaning in academic, administrative, and performance buildings on campus. This position also completes floor care, has good customer service skills, and completes other special projects such as furniture supply moves within the academic buildings on campus. Supervisor may assign other job-related duties not specifically listed under essential tasks.</div><div><br>General and Detail Cleaning – 60%<br>Customer Service – 10%<br>Floor Care – 15%<br>Special Projects – 15%<br><br>This position is a mandatory position as defined in the Adverse Weather and Emergency Event Policy.</div> Facility Services Housekeeping - 56408 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35841 2026-08-31T09:55:21-04:00 2026-08-31T09:55:22-04:00 Assistant Professor of Media Studies <div>The Department of Media Studies at UNC Greensboro invites applications for a Tenure-Track<strong> </strong>Assistant Professor of Media Studies with an emphasis on the<strong> </strong>History and Critical Analysis of Interactive and Emerging Media<strong> to begin August 1, 2027. </strong>We seek a scholar whose research explores the history, theory, and cultural and societal impacts of digital platforms, interactive, and emerging media. The successful candidate will have an established record of scholarship in emerging media research, with expertise in areas such as Cinematic AI, VR/AR/XR, internet subcultures, video games, interactive and immersive media, or virtual production. Candidates should be prepared to teach undergraduate and graduate courses in media theory and studies, including <em>History of Digital Media</em>, <em>Media Theory</em>, <em>Seminar in Media Studies</em>, and <em>Theory and History of Emerging Media</em>. Responsibilities include ongoing scholarly and professional activity, and service to the department, college, and university.</div> Media Studies - 12226 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35478 2026-07-22T12:09:10-04:00 2026-07-22T12:09:11-04:00 Administrative Support Specialist <div>As a part of the Bryan School’s budgetary team, the primary purpose of this <strong>Administrative Support Specialist</strong> is to provide skilled and accurate support for the school’s financial operations. Reporting to the Business Officer, this individual will be tasked with navigating the University’s procurement and accounts payable processes, insuring compliance with policies, documentation needs, and prescribed deadlines. The position also carries some personnel responsibilities in terms of leave management and time entry, serving as a content expert for internal constituents.<br><br>For success in this position, the individual will need strong analytical skills, comfort using data platforms, and a high degree of accuracy/attention to detail. As this is a team-oriented role, individual must be able to work well with others and provide excellent ‘customer’ service whether interacting with internal constituents or external vendors.<br><br>For more information on position, please see key responsibilities section.<br><br></div> Dean's Office - BE - 11801 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/31600 2025-03-24T16:18:11-04:00 2025-03-24T16:18:12-04:00 Lifeguard <div>The lifeguard position is responsible for ensuring the safety of swimmers and participants by monitoring water activities, enforcing safety rules, and providing emergency assistance when necessary. Lifeguards are responsible for educating all patrons of pool policies and procedures to maintain the safety of all people using the pool and or waterfront. Strong communication skills, physical fitness, and the ability to remain calm under pressure are essential for success in this role.</div> Recreation and Wellness - 44801 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35723 2026-08-18T12:25:34-04:00 2026-08-18T12:25:34-04:00 Assistant Professor of Information, Library, & Research Sciences <div><strong>Position Summary <br></strong>Candidates with a specialization in collection development and collection management are preferred. Other areas of interest will also be considered, including the following:</div><ul><li>Digital resource management</li><li>Contracting, licensing, budgeting, and vendor relations</li><li>Information access issues related to digital collections</li><li>Partnerships, collaboration, and outreach with information organizations</li><li>Intellectual Freedom and Intellectual Property</li><li>Special libraries</li><li>Leadership and advocacy</li><li>Emerging technologies and digital equity</li><li>Community engagement with wide range of user communities</li><li>Other areas of focus related to collection development and collection management</li></ul><div><br><strong>Responsibilities</strong></div><ul><li>Participate in instruction, research, publication, and other scholarly activities.</li><li>Teach in synchronous, online environments primarily at the graduate level, with opportunities to teach face-to-face in the undergraduate program as well.</li><li>Mentor and advise graduate students.</li><li>Provide service to the department, school, university, profession, and community.</li></ul> Info/Library/Research/Science - 12024 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35284 2026-06-26T14:25:12-04:00 2026-06-26T14:25:13-04:00 Admissions Counselor <div>The primary purpose of this position is to function as an Admissions Counselor for for the Office of Undergraduate Admissions. This position will recruit and cultivate prospects, applicants, and admitted students through direct participation in a variety of activities, articulate admissions procedures and requirements to prospective students, parents and counselors, evaluate credentials and make independent decisions regarding individuals’ candidacies for admission to UNCG, and positively affect admitted students’ decisions to matriculate to UNCG.</div> Undergraduate Admissions - 10202 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35897 2026-09-04T11:09:55-04:00 2026-09-04T11:09:56-04:00 Steam Plant Operator (Journey) <div><strong>Re-Post, Previous Applicants Need Not Re-Apply, Still Under Consideration<br></strong><br>Primary duties of the position include:</div><ul><li>Observe, monitor, and operate one (1) 40,000-pound-per-hour and three (3) 50,000-pound-per-hour boilers and all related boiler plant machinery.</li><li>Operate the Computerized Boiler Control System.</li><li>Perform both corrective and preventive maintenance as required, to ensure a smooth and constant flow of steam to the campus around the clock.</li><li>Other duties as determined by the supervisor.</li><li>The Department offers training for this position. We're seeking applicants who have a safety-first mindset with basic mechanical and electrical knowledge in which they can build upon their current skill set.</li></ul> Utility Operations - 56406 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/32982 2025-10-03T17:25:56-04:00 2025-10-03T17:25:56-04:00 Collaboration Coordinator - West <div>The Collaboration Coordinator West will foster collaboration and advocate for Family Voice &amp; Choice in partnership with other service delivery systems, State agencies, and other relevant stakeholders, including the Department of Public Instruction and SAMHSA-sponsored national agencies with a focus on the western region of NC.<br><br></div><div>The Collaboration Coordinator also will work to establish a formal network or directory of different family, youth, and/or young-adult led organizations or roles within organizations across the State. This network or directory will help to facilitate future additional collaboration and coordination of individuals working to elevate the voice and perspectives of families, youths, and young adults across the state and help to make it easier than it is currently to identify who is engaged in this work throughout North Carolina.<br><br></div><div>The dedicated Coordination and Collaboration role within the Family and Youth Support and Education Program will be critical to the program’s ability to support local and State Collaboratives, while also remaining true to the SOC Values and Principles.</div> Center-Youth-Families & Comm - 11504 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35850 2026-08-31T13:52:10-04:00 2026-08-31T13:52:10-04:00 Building and Environmental Technician <div>The position is responsible for general and detail cleaning in academic, administrative, and performance buildings on campus. This position also completes floor care, has good customer service skills, and completes other special projects such as furniture supply moves within the academic buildings on campus. Supervisor may assign other job-related duties not specifically listed under essential tasks.<br><br>General and Detail Cleaning – 60%<br>Customer Service – 10%<br>Floor Care – 15%<br>Special Projects – 15%<br><br>This position is a mandatory position as defined in the Adverse Weather and Emergency Event Policy.</div> Facility Services Housekeeping - 56408 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35560 2026-07-30T00:16:58-04:00 2026-07-30T00:17:00-04:00 Coordinator, Fitness Operations <div>Under the direction and supervision of the Assistant Director of Fitness, the Coordinator, Fitness Operations is responsible for the coordination and management of the fitness spaces in the 216,000 sq ft. Leonard J. Kaplan Center for Wellness. The Coordinator, Fitness Operations also directly supervises and develops a team of approximately 30–40 part-time student employees through recruitment, hiring, onboarding, scheduling, training, evaluating, and ongoing professional development. The position is responsible for maintaining service excellence by ensuring staff are knowledgeable in customer service, equipment usage, emergency response procedures, and risk management practices.</div> Recreation and Wellness - 44801 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35900 2026-09-04T12:57:55-04:00 2026-09-04T12:57:56-04:00 Early Childhood Teacher <div><strong>Re-Post, Previous Applicants Need Not Re-Apply, Still Under Consideration<br></strong><br>Early Childhood Education Teachers in the Child Care Education Program are responsible for curriculum planning in classrooms for young children, maintaining licensing and accreditation standards, and creating a respectful high quality classroom environment. Additionally, they provide appropriate guidance for university students working in their classrooms.</div> Human Devlp and Family Studies - 12403 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35784 2026-08-21T00:00:49-04:00 2026-08-21T00:00:50-04:00 Unit Hardware/Software Support Analyst <div>The primary purpose of this position is to provide technology support services to the faculty, staff, and graduate teaching assistants within the Bryan School at UNCG. This includes maintaining the entire inventory of computer equipment for the area, assisting with grant-funded research through the installation, maintenance, problem-solving, and software support of equipment and laboratories, contribute to unit decision making on technological issues, provide one-on-one IT support for faculty, staff, and graduate teaching assistants, maintain unit teaching and research labs, if applicable, and assists with data management and data recovery. Work requires strong communication skills and an ability to effectively interact with a broad range of end-users, with an ability to use a variety of technical resources for providing this support.<br><br>Department-specific duties that may be included:<br><br>Endpoint Support:</div><ul><li>Provide training to faculty and staff on software, hardware, and network systems use in alignment with school and university policies.</li><li>Collaborate with ITS Security to ensure that restricted data (e.g., BLS, DOE, DoD) handled by faculty and staff is managed in compliance with contractual requirements, including oversight of external audits as well as adherence to ITS security standards and university policies.</li><li>Contribute as member of project teams, offering technical guidance and support as needed.</li></ul><div><br></div><div>Consulting:</div><ul><li>Collaborate with ITS Engineering, Security, Networking, CHiP, and Application Management teams to ensure adherence to ITS infrastructure on the below consulting activities.</li><li>Manage access to and integration of data storage systems within the school.</li><li>Provide consultation on faculty hardware and software needs, including requirements for externally funded grants; identify gaps where standard equipment or software is insufficient, recommend alternatives, and assist with required pre-purchase reviews.</li><li>Design and support the implementation of long-term strategies for customized system functionality (e.g., Consumer Apparel and Retail Studies lab technology, USS and Graduate Programs student data systems, ISSCM specialized educational needs).</li></ul> Info Technology Services - 23101 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35309 2026-07-01T00:01:10-04:00 2026-07-01T00:01:11-04:00 Temp Pool for Research/Lab Technician <div>The University of North Carolina at Greensboro is a public, coeducational, doctoral-granting, residential university chartered in 1891. It is one of the three original institutions of The University of North Carolina System.<br><br>The Department of Human Resources is seeking qualified individuals for temporary Research / Lab Technician positions that may become available on campus.<br><br>When a UNCG Department is in need of a temporary Research / Lab Technician, qualified applicants who have applied to this temporary pool will be considered.<br><br>Positions will provide support to experimental processes in a laboratory, clinic, field, and/or teaching environment.<br><br>Duties include, but are not limited to: Conducting research experiments Collecting and summarizing research data Providing proper laboratory/study subject care.</div> Human Resources - 58401 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/33841 2026-01-06T15:27:45-05:00 2026-01-06T15:27:46-05:00 Lecturers/Visiting Faculty/Clinical Faculty <div><strong>The University of North Carolina at Greensboro<br><br>LECTURERS/VISITING FACULTY/CLINICAL FACULTY</strong><br><br><strong>The Positions</strong><br>The University of North Carolina at Greensboro (UNCG) occasionally seeks applicants for full-time, term appointments as lecturers, visiting faculty, clinical faculty (School of Nursing, School of Education), academic professional track (College of Arts &amp; Sciences, School of Music, Theatre and Dance, School of Health and Human Sciences). These are non-tenure-track appointments that include the possibility of renewal based on factors including, but not limited to, continued need, satisfactory performance, and availability of funding. The positions may be day or evening. In many cases, the minimum degree required is the doctorate or terminal degree; the Master’s degree may be appropriate in other instances, based on the requirements of the position. Demonstrated ability to work effectively in an academic setting that is ethnically/culturally diverse is highly desirable.<br><br><strong>For the 2026-2027 academic year</strong>, positions in the following disciplines and departments may be available.<br><br><strong>Dean, College of Arts and Sciences (UNCG, P. O. Box 26170, Greensboro, NC 27402-6170)</strong><br>African American and Diaspora Studies; Liberal &amp; Professional Studies (Liberal &amp; Interdisciplinary Studies, Professional Studies, Religious Studies, International &amp; Global Studies, and Videogaming/Esports); Biology; Chemistry and Biochemistry; Ancient Mediterranean Studies and Archaeology; Communication Studies; Computer Science; English; Freshman Seminars Program; Geography; History; Interior Architecture; Languages, Literatures, and Cultures (Spanish, French, German, Japanese, and American Sign Language); Mathematics and Statistics; Media Studies; Philosophy; Physics and Astronomy; Political Science; Psychology; Sociology, Criminology, and Justice Studies; Women’s, Gender and Sexuality Studies Program.<br><br><strong>Dean, Bryan School of Business and Economics (UNCG, P. O. Box 26170, Greensboro, NC 27402-6165)</strong><br>Accounting and Finance; Consumer, Apparel, and Retail Studies; Economics; Information Systems and Supply Chain Management; Management; Marketing, Entrepreneurship, Hospitality, and Tourism.<br><br><strong>Dean, School of Education (UNCG, P. O. Box 26170, Greensboro, NC 27402-6170)</strong><br>Counseling and Educational Development; Specialized Education Services; Information, Library, and Research Sciences; Educational Leadership and Cultural Foundations; Teacher Education and Higher Education.<br><br><strong>Dean, School of Health and Human Sciences (UNCG, P. O. Box 26170, Greensboro, NC 27402-6170)</strong><br>Communication Sciences and Disorders; Community and Therapeutic Recreation; Human Development and Family Studies; Genetic Counseling; Gerontology; Kinesiology; Nutrition; Public Health Education; Social Work, and Peace and Conflict Studies.<br><br><strong>Dean, College of Visual and Performing Arts (UNCG, PO Box 26170, Greensboro, NC 27402-6170)</strong><br>Various needs in art, arts administration, dance, music, and theatre.<br><br><strong>Dean, School of Nursing (UNCG, P. O. Box 26170, Greensboro, NC 27402-6170)</strong><br>Professional Nursing Education; Advanced Nursing Education and various needs related to nursing education, administration, and clinical practice.</div><div><br><strong>Dean, Joint School of Nanoscience and Nanoengineering (2907 East Gate City Blvd, Greensboro, NC 27401)</strong><br>Various needs in nanoscience education.</div> Office of the Provost - 10101 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35852 2026-08-31T14:30:32-04:00 2026-08-31T14:30:33-04:00 Project Technician <div>This position is mainly responsible for completing various projects on campus, including, but not limited to; floor care, furniture moves, inclement weather coverage, absentee coverage, upholstery cleaning and deep cleaning of restrooms/locker rooms. This position also completes general and detail cleaning in academic, administrative, and performance buildings on campus. In addition, his position also provides good customer service and completes special projects as mentioned previously. Supervisor may assign other job-related duties not specifically listed under essential tasks.<br><br>This position is a mandatory position as defined in the Adverse Weather and Emergency Event Policy.</div> Facility Services Housekeeping - 56408 https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35589 2026-07-31T16:01:46-04:00 2026-07-31T16:01:46-04:00 Program Specialist <div>The Program Specialist position will provide training and local coaching support in the implementation of High Fidelity Wraparound to sites including but not exclusive to Tiered Care Coordination pilot sites and SOC sites. This position includes training, coaching and organizational support. The position will stationed from home with frequent travel to UNCG and statewide.</div> Center-Youth-Families & Comm - 11504"
    },
