ent Communications 000348 University Communications - 33901 Administration - Staff Internal and External The Director, Office of Enrollment Communications, will serve as the primary strategic leader for the University’s enrollment marketing efforts. The director will closely collaborate with leadership in the Division of Enrollment Management, The Graduate School, the Division of Student Success, University Communications, and various academic units to develop data-driven marketing strategies that... View Details Bookmark Systems and Infrastructure Generalist 000331 University Registrar's Office - 10204 Staff Internal and External Reporting to the Assistant Registrar for Systems and Infrastructure, the Systems and Infrastructure Generalist is a member of the Registrar’s Systems and Reporting team and serves within the University Registrar’s Office (URO) as the webmaster, report support, data specialist, and systems technician. This position actively participates in implementing and testing new tools, workflow processes, ... View Details Bookmark Academic Recovery Coordinator 000146 & 999617 Students First Office - 10918 Administration - Staff Internal and External Reporting to the Associate Director of Academic Recovery, the Academic Recovery Coordinator will collaborate with other members of the AR Team to coordinate, implement, and assess ARS 100 and 120, the academic recovery interventions for new students who fall on Academic Probation and Academic Suspension. The ARC serves as the academic coach for an assigned load of ARS 100 and ARS 120 students. ... View Details Bookmark Project Manager (Journey) 999513 Facilities D&C-Departmental - 56411 Administration - Staff Internal and External This position is responsible for comprehensive and simultaneous Project Management of multiple UNCG projects of various sizes. Projects will range in value from less than $30K up to and potentially exceeding the $4M threshold for full NC State Construction Office oversight. The purpose and intent of this position is to execute the following duties for assigned projects: (a) act as agent for the... View Details Bookmark Salesforce Application Administrator 997944 Info Technology Services - 23101 Staff Internal and External This position serves as the institutional Application Administrator and IT System Administrator for University Advancement’s Kindsight Ascend CRM, built on Salesforce. The role partners closely with Advancement Operations, frontline fundraisers, and campus stakeholders to translate fundraising and engagement needs into scalable, secure, and well-governed CRM functionality.System administrators ... View Details Bookmark Assistant Professor of Media Production 1321 Media Studies - 12226 Tenure Stream Internal and External The Department of Media Studies at UNC Greensboro invites applications for a Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Media Production with an emphasis on Virtual Production and Emerging Media to begin August 1, 2027. This position focuses on Media Production with a specific emphasis on Emerging Media technologies. In addition to filmmaking, this position includes other media production with emergin... View Details Bookmark Academic Records Specialist 000423 University Registrar's Office - 10204 Staff Internal and External Reporting to the Assistant Registrar, the Academic Records Specialist is responsible for degree clearance support; tracking of degree progress, certification of graduation for undergraduate students; and serves as a point of contact for the degree clearance area. This position communicates with students, advisors, and other faculty and staff to ensure that graduation applicants have met the req... View Details Bookmark Collaboration Coordinator - Special populations 998035 Center-Youth-Families & Comm - 11504 Research Internal and External The Collaboration Coordinator-Special Populations will foster collaboration and advocate for Family Voice & Choice in partnership with other service delivery systems, State agencies, and other relevant stakeholders, including the Department of Public Instruction and SAMHSA-sponsored national agencies with a focus on historically underserved populations in NC.The Collaboration Coordinator al... View Details Bookmark Assistant/Associate Professor 001353 Counseling and Edu Development - 12003 Tenure Stream Internal and External Faculty in the Department of Counseling and Educational Development (CED) in the School of Education at The University of North Carolina at Greensboro seek a colleague for a tenure line Assistant/Associate Professor with a Clinical Mental Health or Couple and Family specialization, with a particular emphasis on addictions. We are searching for a team-oriented individual who would contribute to ... View Details Bookmark Program Specialist 998449 Center-Youth-Families & Comm - 11504 Research Internal and External The Program Specialist position will provide training and local coaching support in the implementation of High Fidelity Wraparound to sites including but not exclusive to Tiered Care Coordination pilot sites and SOC sites. This position includes training, coaching and organizational support. The position will stationed from home with frequent travel to UNCG and statewide. View Details Bookmark Testing Accommodations Proctor Graduate Assistant - 2026-2027 Acad Achievement Ctr - 10913 Graduate Assistant 10/01/2026 The term Graduate Assistant is the umbrella term that encompasses all types of GA appointments. Graduate Assistants are employed by the University to teach, conduct research, or assist with administrative duties in departments and non-academic units. Every attempt is made to assign Graduate Assistants to positions that are directly related to the student’s field of study or that provide the opp... View Details Bookmark Graduate Program Advisor 997943 MBA Office - 11808 Staff Internal and External The Graduate Academic Advisor position is a permanent position that will report to the A