    "https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35870": {
      "title": "UNC Greensboro Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor of Psychology",
      "description": "UNC Greensboro Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor of Psychology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Current UNCG Employee Log In UNC System Careers Assistant Professor of Psychology Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. We will begin reviewing applications on October 15, 2027 and will continue until the position is filled. More information may be obtained from Dr. Ethan Zell, Chair of the Social Search Committee (email: e_zell@uncg.edu). For additional information or to apply for this position (999406), please visit our website at https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/ . UNCG is a Minority Serving Institution. UNCG and the Psychology Department foster an environment of collaboration across departments and schools and support community-engaged research. UNCG is located in Greensboro, the largest city in North Carolina’s Piedmont Triad region and the third-most populous city in the state. Greensboro is a vibrant city with nearly 300,000 residents and more than 47,000 college students and is known for its expansive parks and greenway system, arts, music, and sports. UNCG is an EOE/AA/M/F/D/V employer. Applicants should submit: A cover letter, including the applicant’s name, current title/institution, a brief description of the applicant’s research focus, and a brief statement describing their fit with our department. A CV. A research statement with up to 1500 words on the applicant’s past research and future research goals if selected for the position. A teaching statement (up to 1000 words) that includes their teaching and mentoring style, courses they would be prepared and excited to teach in our department, and the candidate’s experience or perspective on teaching and mentoring at the undergraduate and graduate level. Up to 3 representative publications. Candidates will arrange for 3 letters of recommendation when completing their application. Posting Details Position Information Position Number 999406 Functional Title Assistant Professor of Psychology Position Type Tenure Stream Position Eclass FC - Faculty 9 month Non Leave earn University Information Located in North Carolina’s third largest city, UNC Greensboro is among the most diverse, learner-centered public research universities in the state, with 18,000 students in eight colleges and schools pursuing more than 150 areas of undergraduate and over 200 areas of graduate study. UNCG continues to be recognized nationally for academic excellence, access, and affordability. UNCG is ranked No. 1 most affordable institution in North Carolina for net cost by the N.Y. Times and No. 1 in North Carolina for social mobility by The Wall Street Journal — helping first-generation and lower-income students find paths to prosperity. Designated an Innovation and Economic Prosperity University by the Association of Public and Land-grant Universities, UNCG is a community-engaged research institution with a portfolio of more than $67M in research and creative activity. The University’s 2,600 staff help create an annual economic impact for the Piedmont Triad region in excess of $1B. Primary Purpose of the Organizational Unit The Department of Psychology consists of 28 full-time faculty and offers a BA and BS in psychology, including Disciplinary Honors, an MA in experimental psychology, and a PhD in clinical, cognitive, developmental, and social psychology (see https://psy.uncg.edu/ for more information). Position Summary The Department of Psychology at UNC Greensboro invites applications for a tenure-track position in Social Psychology (Assistant Professor) to begin August 1, 2027. We seek someone to join an active and collaborative department. The Department of Psychology consists of 28 full-time faculty and offers a BA and BS in psychology, including Disciplinary Honors, an MA in experimental psychology, and a PhD in clinical, cognitive, developmental, and social psychology (see https://psy.uncg.edu/ for more information). The doctoral program in Social Psychology consists of four faculty who provide individualized training in research and statistical methods. We have ongoing expertise on topics such as close relationships, social cognition, social perception, motivation, self and identity, and aesthetics/creativity. We welcome applications from any area of social/personality psychology. We are especially interested in candidates with expertise in both of the following topics: health/well-being and social cognition. More specifically, we seek scholars who study how people think, reason, and make health-related decisions as well as decisions that may more broadly affect their environments and social worlds. The successful candidate will also be expected to contribute coursework and research experiences to an interdisciplinary BA in Health, Medicine, and Society ( HMS ). All applicants should show evidence of a strong independent research program, potential for external funding, a commitment to working with students from diverse backgrounds, and potential for excellence in graduate and undergraduate teaching. Candidates must hold or anticipate a PhD in psychology or a related field by August 1, 2027. Minimum Qualifications Applicants must have or anticipate having a Ph.D. in Psychology or a related field by August 1, 2027. Preferred Qualifications Tenure Status Tenure Track Special Instructions to Applicants We will begin reviewing applications on October 15, 2027 and will continue until the position is filled. More information may be obtained from Dr. Ethan Zell, Chair of the Social Search Committee (email: e_zell@uncg.edu). For additional information or to apply for this position (999406), please visit our website at https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/ . UNCG is a Minority Serving Institution. UNCG and the Psychology Department foster an environment of collaboration across departments and schools and support community-engaged research. UNCG is located in Greensboro, the largest city in North Carolina’s Piedmont Triad region and the third-most populous city in the state. Greensboro is a vibrant city with nearly 300,000 residents and more than 47,000 college students and is known for its expansive parks and greenway system, arts, music, and sports. UNCG is an EOE /AA/M/F/D/V employer. Applicants should submit: A cover letter, including the applicant’s name, current title/institution, a brief description of the applicant’s research focus, and a brief statement describing their fit with our department. A CV. A research statement with up to 1500 words on the applicant’s past research and future research goals if selected for the position. A teaching statement (up to 1000 words) that includes their teaching and mentoring style, courses they would be prepared and excited to teach in our department, and the candidate’s experience or perspective on teaching and mentoring at the undergraduate and graduate level. Up to 3 representative publications. Candidates will arrange for 3 letters of recommendation when completing their application. Recruitment Range Salary is competitive and commensurate with experience. Org #-Department Psychology - 12215 Job Open Date 09/02/2026 For Best Consideration Date 10/15/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes FTE 1.000 Type of Appointment Permanent Time Limited Duration Number of Months per Year 9 FLSA ADA Checklist ADA Checklist \"R\" for Rare (0-30%),\r\n\"O\" for Occasional (30-60%),\r\n\"F\" for Frequent (60-90%),\r\n\"C\" for Constant (90-100%). Physical Effort Hand Movement-Repetitive Motions - O, Hand Movement-Grasping - F, Finger Dexterity - O, Reading - C, Writing - C, Standing - F, Sitting - F, Walking - F, Reaching - O Work Environment Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References Teaching Philosophy Writing Sample(s) Research Statement Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate how you learned of the vacant position for which you are applying: UNCGjobsearch Website Greensboro News & Record Carolina Peacemaker Other Newspaper The Chronicle of Higher Education Inside Higher Ed Other Professional Journal NCWorks.gov UNC System Job Board Other Online Job Board Personal Networking Other * If you selected \"Other\", please provide the name of the resource here. (Open Ended Question) * Are you eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship? Yes No * Will you now or in the future require visa sponsorship for employment at the University of North Carolina in Greensboro? Yes No UNCG Human Resources UNC Greensboro 723 Kenilworth St. Greensboro, NC 27402-6170 Telephone 336.334.5009 Fax 336.334.5585 Back to top Copyright © 2025. UNC Greensboro. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
