    "https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35855": {
      "title": "UNC Greensboro Employment Opportunities | Assistant Director, Building and Environmental Services",
      "description": "UNC Greensboro Employment Opportunities | Assistant Director, Building and Environmental Services Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Current UNCG Employee Log In UNC System Careers Assistant Director, Building and Environmental Services Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Number 004030 Functional Title Assistant Director, Building and Environmental Services Position Type Staff Position Eclass EP - EHRA 12 mo leave earning University Information Located in North Carolina’s third largest city, UNC Greensboro is among the most diverse, learner-centered public research universities in the state, with 18,000 students in eight colleges and schools pursuing more than 150 areas of undergraduate and over 200 areas of graduate study. UNCG continues to be recognized nationally for academic excellence, access, and affordability. UNCG is ranked No. 1 most affordable institution in North Carolina for net cost by the N.Y. Times and No. 1 in North Carolina for social mobility by The Wall Street Journal — helping first-generation and lower-income students find paths to prosperity. Designated an Innovation and Economic Prosperity University by the Association of Public and Land-grant Universities, UNCG is a community-engaged research institution with a portfolio of more than $67M in research and creative activity. The University’s 2,600 staff help create an annual economic impact for the Piedmont Triad region in excess of $1B. Primary Purpose of the Organizational Unit Facilities Operations has the responsibility of providing a wide range of services to the entire UNCG campus. Services include all aspects of corrective and preventive maintenance, operations, grounds maintenance, housekeeping, utility infrastructure maintenance and operations, business operations, safety, regulatory compliance, project management, and renovations. These duties are conducted for a campus consisting of more than 100 buildings totaling 6 million gross square feet on over 275 acres. Position Summary The Assistant Director of Building and Environmental Services provides leadership and coordination of housekeeping and custodial services across campus facilities, most often within Housing and Residence Life or Facilities Operations. This position supervises subordinate housekeeping supervisors, delivery personnel, set-up crews, floor maintenance assistants, and housekeeping staff to ensure clean, safe, and well-maintained living and learning environments. Managers in this band are responsible for planning, scheduling, and inspecting housekeeping operations; managing equipment and supplies; ensuring compliance with safety and health standards; and aligning housekeeping activities with the University’s operational goals. The role also requires leadership in employee development, performance management, and customer service, with accountability for both daily operations and long-range planning of custodial programs. 30% — Leadership & Housekeeping Operations 20% — Maintenance & Special Projects 15% — Customer Service & Stakeholder Engagement 15% — Contract & Budget Management 10% — Inventory & MRO Stores Oversight 5% — Training & Employee Development 5% — Safety & Compliance This position is a mandatory position as defined in the Adverse Weather and Emergency Event Policy. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree and two years of experience in general facilities work; or equivalent combination of training and experience. All degrees must be received from appropriately accredited institutions. Additional Required Certifications, Licensures, and Certificates Valid Driver’s License Preferred Qualifications Special Instructions to Applicants Recruitment Range $73,778 - $81,975 Org #-Department Facilities Operations - 56404 Job Open Date 08/31/2026 For Best Consideration Date Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes FTE 1.000 Type of Appointment Permanent If time-limited, please specify end date for appointment. Number of Months per Year 12 FLSA Exempt Key Responsibilities ________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________ Percentage Of Time 30% Key Responsibility Leadership & Housekeeping Operations Essential Tasks Provide leadership and coordination of all housekeeping and custodial services across academic, administrative, and residential facilities. Supervise and coordinate the selection, training, and daily scheduling of housekeeping employees. Inspect areas for cleanliness, maintenance needs, and compliance with established service standards. Ensure adequate stock of cleaning materials and manage housekeeping services in line with University goals. Percentage Of Time 20% Key Responsibility Maintenance & Special Projects Essential Tasks Plan and coordinate special housekeeping projects, floor maintenance programs, and set-up/move requests. Partner with Facilities Operations to integrate housekeeping functions with maintenance needs. Investigate and report facility damage, supporting timely corrective action. Percentage Of Time 15% Key Responsibility Customer Service & Stakeholder Engagement Essential Tasks Serve as the primary liaison with Housing & Residence Life staff, supervisors, students, parents, and visitors. Address service concerns, communicate expectations, and maintain strong stakeholder relationships. Percentage Of Time 15% Key Responsibility Contract & Budget Management Essential Tasks Develop, maintain, and reconcile departmental financial records. Manage procurement processes, including requisitioning, receiving, and payment for services and supplies. Monitor budget performance, control costs, and prepare financial reports. Percentage Of Time 10% Key Responsibility Inventory & MRO Stores Oversight Essential Tasks Oversee purchasing, stocking, and maintenance of consumables, equipment parts, and custodial supplies. Maintain inventory control systems (e.g., TMA , Maximo, AiM) and ensure accurate reporting. Provide training for staff on inventory management processes. Percentage Of Time 5% Key Responsibility Training & Employee Development Essential Tasks Develop and implement training programs for housekeeping supervisors and staff. Provide leadership coaching, performance management, and professional development opportunities. Percentage Of Time 5% Key Responsibility Safety & Compliance Essential Tasks Administer safety and health programs, ensuring compliance with OSHA , OSHR , and University standards. Maintain Safety Data Sheet ( SDS ) systems and provide required training. Conduct audits, investigate incidents, and implement corrective actions to mitigate risk. ADA Checklist ADA Checklist R for Rare (0-30%), O for Occasional (30-60%), F for Frequent (60-90%), C for Constant (90-100%). Physical Effort Hand Movement-Repetitive Motions - F, Hand Movement-Grasping, Holding - F, Finger Dexterity - F, Vision-Skilled Trades - F, Reading - F, Writing - F, Eye-hand coordination - F, Vision-Color Distinction - F, Vision-Preparing/Analyzing figures - F, Vision-Visual inspection - F, Vision-Measuring/Assembling at distance close to eye - F, Hearing - C, Talking - F, Standing - O, Sitting - C, Walking - O, Lifting-0-30 lbs. - O, Pushing/Pulling - R, Climbing-Stairs - O, Bending - R, Squatting - R, Reaching - O Work Environment Driving - Car/Truck - R, Inside - C Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV List of References Optional Documents Cover Letter Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate how you learned of the vacant position for which you are applying: UNCGjobsearch Website Greensboro News & Record Carolina Peacemaker Other Newspaper The Chronicle of Higher Education Inside Higher Ed Other Professional Journal NCWorks.gov UNC System Job Board Other Online Job Board Personal Networking Other * If you selected \"Other\", please provide the name of the resource here. (Open Ended Question) * Are you eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship? Yes No * Will you now or in the future require visa sponsorship for employment at the University of North Carolina in Greensboro? Yes No UNCG Human Resources UNC Greensboro 723 Kenilworth St. Greensboro, NC 27402-6170 Telephone 336.334.5009 Fax 336.334.5585 Back to top Copyright © 2025. UNC Greensboro. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/bookmarks?posting_id=35855": {
      "title": "UNC Greensboro Employment Opportunities",
