    "https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35828": {
      "title": "UNC Greensboro Employment Opportunities | Program Assistant - Scheduling Coordinator",
      "description": "UNC Greensboro Employment Opportunities | Program Assistant - Scheduling Coordinator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Current UNCG Employee Log In UNC System Careers Program Assistant - Scheduling Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Number 999002 Functional Title Program Assistant - Scheduling Coordinator Position Type Staff Position Eclass EZ - EHRA Non - Exempt Permanent University Information Located in North Carolina’s third largest city, UNC Greensboro is among the most diverse, learner-centered public research universities in the state, with 18,000 students in eight colleges and schools pursuing more than 150 areas of undergraduate and over 200 areas of graduate study. UNCG continues to be recognized nationally for academic excellence, access, and affordability. UNCG is ranked No. 1 most affordable institution in North Carolina for net cost by the N.Y. Times and No. 1 in North Carolina for social mobility by The Wall Street Journal — helping first-generation and lower-income students find paths to prosperity. Designated an Innovation and Economic Prosperity University by the Association of Public and Land-grant Universities, UNCG is a community-engaged research institution with a portfolio of more than $67M in research and creative activity. The University’s 2,600 staff help create an annual economic impact for the Piedmont Triad region in excess of $1B. Primary Purpose of the Organizational Unit The North Carolina Rated License Assessment Project ( NCRLAP ) is a collaborative project between the NC Division of Child Development and the University of North Carolina at Greensboro. NCRLAP conducts voluntary assessments for child care centers and family child care homes within the NC Star Rated License System. In this way NCRLAP plays a central role in the licensing process of child care facilities Position Summary This position is pivotal in fostering a culture of excellence, demonstrating strong leadership, and significantly impacting the organization’s overall efficiency and effectiveness by supporting NCRLAP staff. The key responsibilities include additional leadership assignments (55%), schedule assessments (25%), budget and financial management (15%), and other duties (5%). Minimum Qualifications HIGH SCHOOL DIPLOMA OR EQUIVALENCY AND ONE YEAR OF RELATED OFFICE EXPERIENCE ; OR EQUIVALENT COMBINATION OF TRAINING AND EXPERIENCE . Additional Required Certifications, Licensures, and Certificates Preferred Qualifications A four -year degree in the Early Childhood Education field with at least 2 years business experience or a four -year degree in Business with at least 2 years of experience in the field of Early Childhood Education or related 4 -year degree. Special Instructions to Applicants Recruitment Range $45,000 to $52,086 Org #-Department Human Devlp and Family Studies - 12403 Job Open Date 08/27/2026 For Best Consideration Date 09/15/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled No FTE 1.000 Type of Appointment Permanent If time-limited, please specify end date for appointment. Number of Months per Year 12 FLSA Non-Exempt Key Responsibilities ________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________ Percentage Of Time 55% Key Responsibility Additional leadership assignments Essential Tasks 1. Administrative support: Perform main office duties and provide administrative support to staff. These duties include scanning, shredding, printing, mailing, processing forms, assisting with DCDEE audits and reports, understanding features of the NCRLAP website, filing, take pictures and assemble ID badges as assigned, and ordering supplies. 2. Technological support: Train and assist NCRLAP employees as needed to use various types of technology. Assist with problems related to software (e.g., Box), office equipment, computers, and place repair orders requested by staff members. Set up equipment for meetings as requested by NCRLAP management. 3. Outreach related activities: Provide assistance to the outreach coordinator, particularly related to online trainings (e.g., upload videos, work with Qualtrics, review training information). 4. Special Projects: Special projects includes activities that NCRLAP staff undertake to innovate and introduce new technology, products, systems, and services (e.g., Making Connections, 3’s Practice Project, research, resource development, activities related to Outreach Assessments). 5. Staff conference organizer: Collaboratively plan, manage, and facilitate NCRLAP’s staff conferences. Typically staff conferences occur twice annually, in the fall and spring. 6. Asset management: Manages equipment, such as computers and printers, particularly as it is given to/received from NCRLAP staff working from home offices. Orders equipment and is charged with keeping current asset management information on our website. Distribute assets to NCRLAP employees as needed and assist with “surplus” equipment; maintain accurate and up to date inventory records on website including annual review of staff asset forms. 7. Password manager: Manage passwords associated with websites and/or accounts used by NCRLAP staff. 8. Website Administrator: Get passwords, access special pages or tools, add/remove members, make changes to certification information, access to most restricted components of our website. Percentage Of Time 25% Key Responsibility Schedule assessments Essential Tasks 1. Schedule various types of assessments (e.g., DCDEE assessments, Outreach Assessment, research, reliability checks, trainings) in accordance with NCRLAP procedures. This includes assigning eligible assessors to assessment based on scale qualifications, proximity, and availability as defined by NCRLAP procedures. 2. Reschedule assessments as needed; help assessors find solutions to ensure that assessments are completed in an efficient and timely manner. 3. Complete other tasks related to scheduling assessments; including maximizing assessor workload, optimizing workload across the entire team of assessors, scan and handle assessment documents, and other office duties. 4. Act as an ambassador and advocate for NCRLAP , fostering connections with ECE professionals, including child care providers, in a manner that cultivates positive relationships and instills trust. Percentage Of Time 15% Key Responsibility Budget and financial management Essential Tasks 1. Budget preparation and planning: Assist the Project Coordinator and other stakeholders (e.g., Principal Investigator) in the development and preparation of annual budgets. Collaborate with Contracts and Grants, other departments (e.g., Accounts Payable), and individuals (e.g., supervisors, PC, APC ) to gather budgetary data for the various budget lines. If needed, assist with mid-year budget revisions (e.g., prepare documentation for C & G). 2. Monitoring and reporting: Track expenditures and ensure they align with the approved budget. Alert management to any significant deviations from the budget. 3. Administrative financial tasks: Handle routine administrative tasks related to budget management. Organize and file budget documents and correspondence. Manage and update budget-related documents and forms (e.g., spreadsheets, expenditures). Make purchases of office supplies and assets (e.g., laptops, computers, monitors) as described in our contract. Maintain detailed records of financial transactions using appropriate financial management system; including UNCG’s financial systems (e.g., Embers Chrome River, pCard, Banner, UNCGenie) and NCRLAP’s website pages related to the budget (e.g., travel vouchers/gift cards, salary information on staff details page). 4. Assist with internal and/or external audits: Prepare documentation and provide information as needed for auditing purposes. Percentage Of Time 5% Key Responsibility Other duties Essential Tasks 1. Complete activities assigned by your supervisor (or their designate); these may include tasks, projects, workgroups, travel, creating resources and so on. 2. Follow UNCG and NCRLAP guidelines, policies and procedures. 3. Consistently perform activities that align with NCRLAP’s mission statement and, when appropriate, act as an ambassador and advocate for NCRLAP . 4. Consistently demonstrate understanding about the importance of Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion and implementing NCRLAP’s Racial Equity Position Statement. ADA Checklist ADA Checklist R for Rare (0-30%), O for Occasional (30-60%), F for Frequent (60-90%), C for Constant (90-100%). Physical Effort Hand Movement-Repetitive Motions - F, Hand Movement-Grasping - O, Finger Dexterity - F, Reading - F, Writing - O, Vision-Preparing/Analyzing figures - O, Hearing - F, Talking - F, Standing - O, Sitting - F, Walking - O, Lifting-0-30 lbs. - O, Climbing-Stairs - R, Bending - O, Reaching - O Work Environment Inside - C Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate how you learned of the vacant position for which you are applying: UNCGjobsearch Website Greensboro News & Record Carolina Peacemaker Other Newspaper The Chronicle of Higher Education Inside Higher Ed Other Professional Journal NCWorks.gov UNC System Job Board Other Online Job Board Personal Networking Other * If you selected \"Other\", please provide the name of the resource here. (Open Ended Question) * Are you eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship? Yes No * Will you now or in the future require visa sponsorship for employment at the University of North Carolina in Greensboro? Yes No * Do you have experience providing administrative or program support in a professional organization? Yes No * Do you have professional experience working in early childhood education or a related field? Yes No * Do you have experience using technology or information systems to manage, organize, or track work-related information? Yes No * Do you have experience coordinating schedules, appointments, or activities involving multiple staff members, locations, or competing priorities? Yes No * Do you have experience with budget management, purchasing, expense tracking, financial records, or similar financial responsibilities? Yes No UNCG Human Resources UNC Greensboro 723 Kenilworth St. Greensboro, NC 27402-6170 Telephone 336.334.5009 Fax 336.334.5585 Back to top Copyright © 2025. UNC Greensboro. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
