    "https://spartantalent.uncg.edu/postings/35807": {
      "title": "UNC Greensboro Employment Opportunities | Administrative Support Specialist",
      "description": "UNC Greensboro Employment Opportunities | Administrative Support Specialist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Current UNCG Employee Log In UNC System Careers Administrative Support Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Number 2679 Functional Title Administrative Support Specialist Position Type Staff Position Eclass EZ - EHRA Non - Exempt Permanent University Information Located in North Carolina’s third largest city, UNC Greensboro is among the most diverse, learner-centered public research universities in the state, with 18,000 students in eight colleges and schools pursuing more than 150 areas of undergraduate and over 200 areas of graduate study. UNCG continues to be recognized nationally for academic excellence, access, and affordability. UNCG is ranked No. 1 most affordable institution in North Carolina for net cost by the N.Y. Times and No. 1 in North Carolina for social mobility by The Wall Street Journal — helping first-generation and lower-income students find paths to prosperity. Designated an Innovation and Economic Prosperity University by the Association of Public and Land-grant Universities, UNCG is a community-engaged research institution with a portfolio of more than $67M in research and creative activity. The University’s 2,600 staff help create an annual economic impact for the Piedmont Triad region in excess of $1B. Primary Purpose of the Organizational Unit The School of Education is committed to creating life-changing opportunities through education by providing transformative learning, leading innovation and discovery, engaging communities, and promoting equity and diversity. Position Summary This position, housed in the Dean’s Office, will provide support to several areas within the School of Education without administrative support. This position will offer support to School of Education’s Dean’s Office, Business Office, Office of Student Success, and Spartan Education Scholars Program. Other duties include initiating personnel actions, budgeting (including processing all payments and travel reimbursements), event planning, customer service, and other office activities. Minimum Qualifications HIGH SCHOOL DIPLOMA OR EQUIVALENCY AND ONE YEAR OF RELATED OFFICE EXPERIENCE ; OR EQUIVALENT COMBINATION OF TRAINING AND EXPERIENCE . Additional Required Certifications, Licensures, and Certificates Preferred Qualifications Previous professional experience with financial management (e.g., purchasing, A/R, data entry/reporting, and account reconciliation). Experience with software platforms including Banner, Chrome River, Excel and other Microsoft tools. Prior experience working in higher education or state/government operations will be considered favorably. Special Instructions to Applicants Recruitment Range $45,834 - $47,209 Org #-Department Dean's Office - ED - 12001 Job Open Date 08/24/2026 For Best Consideration Date 09/11/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes FTE 1.000 Type of Appointment Permanent If time-limited, please specify end date for appointment. Number of Months per Year 12 FLSA Non-Exempt Key Responsibilities ________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________ Percentage Of Time 25% Key Responsibility Budgeting/Financial Management Essential Tasks Maintain all aspects of departmental/program funds; maintain budgets for Other Than Personnel state funds, non-state discretionary funds, expend funds for all departmental business including travel expenses, operational expenses, recruiting and advertising costs, event/conference expenditures; maintain and reconcile PCard transactions; and initiate paperwork for student-related payment actions. Percentage Of Time 20% Key Responsibility Business and office administration/records management Essential Tasks Maintain consistent operation of all departmental administrative business by following and implementing procedures that ensure accurate record-keeping of student, faculty, and employee data, departmental program data, and departmental financial data. Percentage Of Time 20% Key Responsibility Communication/Customer Service Essential Tasks Interact with faculty, staff, students, and business partners via email, telephone, and in person. Write and edit documents, forms, correspondence, explain policies and procedures; and report information as needed. Percentage Of Time 20% Key Responsibility Event Planning /organizing work Essential Tasks Coordinate School of Education and department-sponsored events. Ensure operational policies and procedures are followed. Percentage Of Time 15% Key Responsibility Other Duties Essential Tasks Supports the overall functioning of the Department by performing other duties as assigned. ADA Checklist ADA Checklist R for Rare (0-30%), O for Occasional (30-60%), F for Frequent (60-90%), C for Constant (90-100%). Physical Effort Hand Movement-Repetitive Motions, Hand Movement-Grasping, Reading, Writing, Eye-hand coordination, Hearing, Talking, Standing, Sitting, Walking, Lifting-0-30 lbs. Work Environment Inside Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How many years of Administrative Support experience do you have? Less than 1 year 1 year 2 years 3 years or more * Please indicate how you learned of the vacant position for which you are applying: UNCGjobsearch Website Greensboro News & Record Carolina Peacemaker Other Newspaper The Chronicle of Higher Education Inside Higher Ed Other Professional Journal NCWorks.gov UNC System Job Board Other Online Job Board Personal Networking Other * If you selected \"Other\", please provide the name of the resource here. (Open Ended Question) * Are you eligible to work in the United States without sponsorship? Yes No * Will you now or in the future require visa sponsorship for employment at the University of North Carolina in Greensboro? Yes No UNCG Human Resources UNC Greensboro 723 Kenilworth St. Greensboro, NC 27402-6170 Telephone 336.334.5009 Fax 336.334.5585 Back to top Copyright © 2025. UNC Greensboro. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
